{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information","id":1463892,"title":"After much speculation: some new W5 official information","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-14T15:43:02-07:00","id":1463892,"title":"After much speculation: some new W5 official information","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=2L9Cj3VMHzw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=2L9Cj3VMHzw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=2L9Cj3VMHzw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=2L9Cj3VMHzw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> There you go:<br /> <br /> -11 playable tribes in the crb<br /> -2 tribes who are no more part of the litany. One because it feels like the Garou nation was not doing it right (Stargazers?) and another who fell to its own rage born out of desperation (Red Talons?)<br /> -A new condition opposite to harano <br /> -The umbra becoming much more hostile to werewolves<br /> -No more metis <br /> -The notion that the apocalypse has POSSIBLY come and gone and we are now living in a post apocalyptic world\u2026 and it\u2019s not what we expected<br /> -A stronger focus on renown as the core concept of Werewolf <br /> <br /> Thoughts? Opinions? Unbridled rage? Gloomy melancholy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T15:46:40-07:00","id":1463894,"title":"","content":"the only thing I mildly find intresting is the hey maybe we are post -apoc <br /> <br /> I think I could run with that honestly<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/324-ardenty","name":"ardenty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar324_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T16:13:55-07:00","id":1463901,"title":"","content":"This is already being discussed in other threads, but my basic reaction:<br /> <br /> They have met my exceedingly low expectations for what I thought W5 would look like. I've been waiting to see if W5 can recover from the sloppy roll out of V5 and make WoD 5e something appealing to me. This all rather confirms that's never going to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T16:17:40-07:00","id":1463902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1463901#post1463901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is already being discussed in other threads, but my basic reaction:<br /> <br /> They have met my exceedingly low expectations for what I thought W5 would look like. I've been waiting to see if W5 can recover from the sloppy roll out of V5 and make WoD 5e something appealing to me. This all rather confirms that's never going to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is that you find so underwhelming, exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T16:33:31-07:00","id":1463904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1463902#post1463902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is that you find so underwhelming, exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for Heavy Arms but everything I'm hearing about it points towards a declawing and infantilization of the Garou.<br /> They seem to be trying to remove everything &quot;problematic&quot; about the setting like the Metis or the treatment of Kinfolk and all that will lead to is a less multifaceted universe.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T16:50:59-07:00","id":1463908,"title":"","content":"They are also cutting out the Umbra by making it super hostile and dangerous by default. It's half the setting for crying out loud.<br /> <br /> Another thing that worried me in the stream was referring to gifts being powered by renown and your relationship to spirits. Gifts are just that, gifts. A spirit imbues part of a Garou's own spirit with its blessing and the power the Garou gains is now a permanent part of them.<br /> <br /> You can entreat a spirit for a gift and your rank and renown helps determine how likely the spirit is to choose to help you. This sounds like renown is the resource powering gifts or that you ask a spirit each time to do something which shows a fundamental lack of familiarity or understanding of the old lore and system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T17:02:01-07:00","id":1463910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1463908#post1463908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are also cutting out the Umbra by making it super hostile and dangerous by default. It's half the setting for crying out loud.</div> </div> </div> </div>Half the setting, a third of the Breeds, and at least some portions of the Litany.<br /> <br /> They really took a chainsaw to the setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T17:14:02-07:00","id":1463912,"title":"","content":"Yeah, after 30 years in the fandom I'm gonna punch out. This and the other stuff Justin said shows a fundamental misunderstanding of the themes and core spirit of WtA. Which is fair enough as Justin has had bugger all to do with WtA over the years and the 3? pieces of writing he's done for it emphasise the schlockier and more puerile outer concepts at the expense of the core values of spirituality, dedication and found-family.<br /> <br /> We absolutely do not need an Avatar Storm/Hisil mash up, anyone whose familiar with the material knows that the Umbra is hostile to Garou and does not need 'cranking to 11'.<br /> <br /> Removing Crinos-Born? I can live with it but it does mean a massive retcon of large swathes of history and metaplot or they could do another kludgy metaplot pull like most of the changes in V5.<br /> <br /> The changes to the way renown function just strike me as more change for change sake, Haglust as the opposite of Harano I don't really care about as I think it will be used as often as Harano is in the average campaign which is to say never unless its a plot point for a particular PC or NPC another change for the sake of change.<br /> <br /> Dumping tribes from the nation was shit when it was done to the Stargazers, its still shit. This is the kind of thing PCs should have a hand in trying to prevent not another ' shit happened off-screen here are the consequences, sucks to be you.'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T17:29:23-07:00","id":1463914,"title":"","content":"I'll add something different:<br /> <br /> Going way back to when the nWW team was talking about their future plans, a bunch of us felt that what they really wanted to make was the CofD, but they wanted the brand recognition of the WoD. Martin basically admitted as much.<br /> <br /> V5 haphazardly grabbed from VtR, and some other games, and tried to smash it all together with VtM. I tried to wait and see. The playtests kept demonstrating that they weren't going to make the balancing act work in a fashion I'd like. Then V5 dropped and confirmed it. And then the V5 supplements continued to disappoint.<br /> <br /> W5 seems to repeating all of the same mistakes. Instead of trying to make a WtA for the 2020s, they're grabbing from Forsaken, and the BNS MET WtA book, and the I-already-don't-like-it V5. So what reason do I have to believe W5 is going to fix any of the development processes that created the V5 I don't want?<br /> <br /> What was announced that will actually appeal to me when I can play Forsaken or W20 instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T17:47:01-07:00","id":1463920,"title":"","content":"Furthermore, I would add that part of the fun of Werewolf: The Apocalypse is the fact that the Garou adhere to an entirely different set of values from modern humanity. This cultural identity is what makes them more than just people who can turn into animals.<br /> And W5 seems intent on stripping all of this from the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T18:45:02-07:00","id":1463925,"title":"","content":"Ok, here's my 2 cents as well:<br /> <br /> -11 tribes and 2 tribes becoming non playable \u2192 I'm not happy with this simply because as goofy as they often were tribes (as clans) have a special place in my memories, aside from that a lot of people complained about one tribe or the other back in the day. Stargazers (if they get the boot) went the way of the Beast Courts in Revised because at the time WW felt it could do nothing interesting with them staying in the Garou nation (and wanted to push the breeds, probably). Red Talons (again, IF they are the tribe that falls prey to Haglust, could very well be the Fenrir, Heart of the Forest has a Red Talon character while Fenrir are mistrusted... and them wanting to take action here and now, damn the consequences fits their philosopy pretty well... so it could be the Fenrir) have always been considered problematic by a lot of folks. I'm not one of them though and I happen to think that the Red Talons point of view would be extremely poignant in a &quot;post Apocalypse&quot; setting.<br /> -Haglust \u2192 Seems possibly an interesting concept, it all depends on implementation and I have no problem with the notion that Garou's rage can get them out of their mind if they think the battle for Gaia is truly lost or is going to be lost unless they do SOMETHING (&quot;And what should we do exactly? Something! Anything! Damn you wyrmspawn! Wraaaaagh!&quot;)<br /> -The Umbra is a much scarier place \u2192 Again, depends on implementation. If it's another avatar storm then I don't like it. AS was implemented because WW decided Mages should fight for Earth and not spend all of their time in Horizon Realms. If the Umbra becoming more dangerous is meant to discourage games taking place in the spirit world then it's not a good idea imo. If it's a way to make the Umbra more challenging to PCs but it's still essential for the game then I'm open to the idea.<br /> -No more metis \u2192 Again, I regret the memories but I don't feel like the metis were a defining concept of W:tA. Again, much will depend on implementation. If they just retcon the metis out of existence then it's an atrocity. If instead they recognize the metis used to exist but went extinct after the &quot;event&quot; in the early 2000s then I can live with this change.<br /> -The Apocalypse has come and gone \u2192 This is an interesting idea that lends itself to numerous new concepts without earsing the old ones and possibly give the setting a glimmer of... hope? The fact that saving the world is not about winning a giant cosmic battle and more about rebuilding and defending what was salvaged after said battle is novel and worth exploring imo.<br /> -Renown as the core concept of W:tA. I don't really have an opinion on this. Renown was always a requisite for access to stronger gifts but it wasn't always easy to get right in games (a player does moronic things but at least shows up and plays... are you really going to punish him/her?) and a better way to make it work would certainly be welcome, on the other hand I always felt W.tA was mainly about raging against injustice and doing terrible things for the greater good and I don't really want the focus of the game to shift too far away from those concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T20:01:10-07:00","id":1463937,"title":"","content":"Renown is something I was hoping to see get a redo. Renown isn't well... Renown. It's bookkeeping before you actually get to do something that impresses people (your Rank challenge). The Renown charts encourage far too much farming of small bonuses, to counter all the small negatives you can build up. Outside of a few rare Gifts, you never do anything with Renown besides get enough of it to gain Rank. There's no difference mechanically between a Wisdom 1 and a Wisdom 10 character because what Rank they might qualify for. Other Garou don't know your Renown rating, and most groups don't do the work necessary to make sure there are actual deeds your character's done that others will hear about.<br /> <br /> Forsaken 2e's treatment of Renown is rather appealing: Each dot of Renown is one major deed your character has accomplished, with the assumption that higher dots are only justified by bigger deeds on some level. Renown is also really important to Gifts in a rewarding way. The linked Renown trait adds to Gift usually as a dice-bonus for activation, or be being a variable (like a Gift that adds Purity extra Health for a scene). The Uratha can also do two cool Renown specific mechanics: one where the rest of the pack needs to challenge if they're really worthy of their Renown, but this is to strength the werewolf and gives them a boost to Renown related stuff (If you flare your Wisdom Brands and defend your wisdom to your pack, everyone following your advice or plans gets a +2 dice bonus to resist being swayed off your advice, and you can end the effect to get extra successes on a single Investigation, Medicine, or Occult roll), and the other is a debuff you can smack the target of your pack's current hunt based on your Auspice.<br /> <br /> It's a really slick way to do what the W5 stuff is talking about.. so much so that I'm not sure if they've got something as good or better up their sleeves. I worry they're just going to lift some of this from Forsaken without thinking about how to get it to interact with WtA. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T22:23:24-07:00","id":1463952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1463937#post1463937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Renown is something I was hoping to see get a redo. Renown isn't well... Renown. It's bookkeeping before you actually get to do something that impresses people (your Rank challenge). The Renown charts encourage far too much farming of small bonuses, to counter all the small negatives you can build up. Outside of a few rare Gifts, you never do anything with Renown besides get enough of it to gain Rank. There's no difference mechanically between a Wisdom 1 and a Wisdom 10 character because what Rank they might qualify for. Other Garou don't know your Renown rating, and most groups don't do the work necessary to make sure there are actual deeds your character's done that others will hear about.<br /> <br /> Forsaken 2e's treatment of Renown is rather appealing: Each dot of Renown is one major deed your character has accomplished, with the assumption that higher dots are only justified by bigger deeds on some level. Renown is also really important to Gifts in a rewarding way. The linked Renown trait adds to Gift usually as a dice-bonus for activation, or be being a variable (like a Gift that adds Purity extra Health for a scene). The Uratha can also do two cool Renown specific mechanics: one where the rest of the pack needs to challenge if they're really worthy of their Renown, but this is to strength the werewolf and gives them a boost to Renown related stuff (If you flare your Wisdom Brands and defend your wisdom to your pack, everyone following your advice or plans gets a +2 dice bonus to resist being swayed off your advice, and you can end the effect to get extra successes on a single Investigation, Medicine, or Occult roll), and the other is a debuff you can smack the target of your pack's current hunt based on your Auspice.<br /> <br /> It's a really slick way to do what the W5 stuff is talking about.. so much so that I'm not sure if they've got something as good or better up their sleeves. I worry they're just going to lift some of this from Forsaken without thinking about how to get it to interact with WtA.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They could handle it more like the central tempers in pre-C20 Land of Eight Million Dreams, where an appropriate milestone got a check mark, and ten checks increased the trait by one. Deeds of various virtues worked similarly in Weapons of the Gods, where they were a part of the process of cultivation needed to clear another power rank.<br /> <br /> Or, if the emphasis is on war over the hunt, make sure that they have appropriate categories that don't overlap with Forsaken at all. It'd be a bit of a break, but you could rearrange the salient categories across the Garou and various Fera to make that happen, or just make whole new ones that aren't Purity et al.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T23:34:12-07:00","id":1463968,"title":"","content":"My thoughts:<br /> <br /> - 11 tribes/no more part of litany - It doesn't matter for me which tribe will be unplayable, because cutting off one of the original tribe is painful for me, I have bad feeling that they will remove Red Talons cause they don't know what to do with them. And new tribe? Confederacy of offshoots from every tribe stricken by the new ,,plague&quot; ? Or for example they would cut off Bone Gnawers cause it's incorrect to play a homeless man? Fenris? Children of Gaia? Which is the best tribe for any of You You like to play and love? And now it might be unplayable? Any choice is bad. No litany and law? So anarch tribes? Oh $%$#%$#%# off.<br /> <br /> - The umbra becoming much more hostile to werewolves - Forsaken 3rd edition. Split the games, the theme, don't make them similar.<br /> <br /> - No more metis - And here we are, 21 century, political correctness. Someone said somewhere ,,you have right to feel offended.&quot; So I'm exercising my right to be offended. Why not metis? It's a huge bow to who? I've read a lot of posts in youtube and even here from liberal people who doesn't like the idea of cutting metis from the game, cause it's a strong part of it like the litany. It's FAR more better to forbid playing them then retconing or ereasing their existance. If the world is in miserable state as they said in video why would suddenly Luna or Gaia or other power make them disappear. In truly shitty world their number would rise, garou need troops, And what with Dancers ,,famous&quot; with their metis? Their cannon fodder. No metis at all? Funny. Very.<br /> <br /> - Pure Breed - another politcal incorrectness? All right change the name but don't take away garou lineage, a thing they were proud off. Heroic Lineage or something similar - Heavy Arms mentione that earlier is good example.<br /> <br /> - Renown and Gifts. If the creators doesn't want to continue renown mechanics from earlier editions please make it from the scratch, new one, but don't copy it from Forsaken, it's different game, different werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> And yes I will buy it cause it's my first and most beloved game. Even if the game will be full of off-putting ideas. I'm from concrete fandom fan base. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 10-15-2021, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T00:15:36-07:00","id":1463974,"title":"","content":"Cannibalization of Forsaken, which now seems to be' only a corpse from where WtA can feed.<br /> <br /> Renown gifts, hostile umbra, and so on.<br /> <br /> Very sad. Forsaken is nice because its not apocalypse especially 2nd ed.<br /> Now they could be' really closer. <br /> <br /> Metis out and &quot;fuck other werewolves is ok&quot; because &quot;werewolves in 2021 have other things to worry about&quot;? <br /> MASSIVE blow to the social structure and to one of the main dramma of the whole setting.<br /> <br /> The fact that a game is horror and mature doesnt mean it cant be' inclusive. <br /> <br /> <br /> Mixed feelings about more multicultural tribes and remove of pure breed. <br /> <br /> I didnt like what I heard .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T00:49:32-07:00","id":1463976,"title":"","content":"Some Breed, like Nuwisha, had the Renown worked into Gifts, like for example the length an effect lasted was tied to one specific Renown value. I found that okay and Garou could have that, too.<br /> <br /> With the removal of Pure Breed I find it okay if Renown plays a greater role in social interaction. And with the CoD-Attributes, Resolve and Composure, I can see Renown as a Pure Breed Like bonus when dealing in contested rolls with other supernaturals or just garou. Something like that...<br /> <br /> Like I said, I would like an overhaul of the mechanics very much, but the I'm opposed to Setting Changes for the most part. So, I hope the new mechanics are as Setting agnostic as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T02:57:32-07:00","id":1463987,"title":"","content":"The tricky part is trying to figure out who this is designed to appeal to, It's quite reductionist in it's outlook and doesnt really enhance the game in any discernable ways. New players won't really benifit from it and it's just going to annoy established player were it might even escalate to fandom splits ala v5 vs v20. Cui Bono? as they say.<br /> <br /> Also I'm slightly bemused at the removal of metis as though it was a tabboo subject, the subtext of metis was incest closed breeding genetic issues and that's genrally tabboo unless i missed that contigency at the last pride march I attended. Love who you love by all means but railing your mother is supremely fucked up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-15-2021, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T03:27:22-07:00","id":1463994,"title":"","content":"I think the big problems (besides the name) are the levels of abuse heaped (physical, social, and spiritual) on a child who's only crime was being born is a pretty nasty subject to have a one of the three default Breed's whole deal. As WtA proved with the other Fera, there are a lot of ways to handle the concept that doesn't push on something quite so sensitive. The whole &quot;spiritual incest&quot; aspect is also not great... esp. with how common it seems to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T04:26:33-07:00","id":1464000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1463994#post1463994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the big problems (besides the name) are the levels of abuse heaped (physical, social, and spiritual) on a child who's only crime was being born is a pretty nasty subject to have a one of the three default Breed's whole deal. As WtA proved with the other Fera, there are a lot of ways to handle the concept that doesn't push on something quite so sensitive. The whole &quot;spiritual incest&quot; aspect is also not great... esp. with how common it seems to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience with playing and hosting Werewolf is that the players who made Metis characters were the same people who created a Thin Blood when playing Vampire.<br /> <br /> They wanted to experience that social rejection to then rise above it and prove the naysayers wrong But now they don't even want players to think about how the circunstances of their birth might affect their station making the Garou Nation a social utopia that has never existed among humanity.<br /> This is just babyproofing Werewolf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T05:02:40-07:00","id":1464006,"title":"","content":"Metis issue - It could be also escape. Why? In Vampire they cut a lot of disciplines and combined some of them. Werewolf gift list seems to be larger - &gt; breed , auspice, tribe and next from for example book of the city and tribebooks. Abandoning metis makes the list shorter.<br /> And maby what I'm saying doesn't have any sense cause they will rebuild gift system.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T05:04:20-07:00","id":1464008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464000#post1464000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My experience with playing and hosting Werewolf is that the players who made Metis characters were the same people who created a Thin Blood when playing Vampire.<br /> <br /> They wanted to experience that social rejection to then rise above it and prove the naysayers wrong But now they don't even want players to think about how the circunstances of their birth might affect their station making the Garou Nation a social utopia that has never existed among humanity.<br /> This is just babyproofing Werewolf</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it is more making sure those who are disabled not having to deal with ableism during their fun time. I'm disabled and I like playing crinos-born, but I also have not been subjected to abuse over my disability.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, the inspirations for the breed are Quasimodo, Basket Case, Bat Boy from the Goonies, etc. Someone physically malformed who is an outsider and bitter about it. That 'deformed freak in the attic' trope is no longer something tolerated.<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> once noted that a metis character could also make other players uncomfortable, as they did not want to heap on abuse to a disabled person.<br /> <br /> Basically, I don't feel it is babyproofing as much as just addressing something that was once okay but no longer is because we are more aware of having disabled players around.<br /> <br /> Mind, I rather not have the breed removed, but I understand why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 10-15-2021, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T05:21:36-07:00","id":1464010,"title":"","content":"In my opinion garou at young age before first change are in similar position.<br /> <br /> Homid are often too agressive, weird, psychotic or worse (like long forgoten line of Dancers). In Book of Weaver, DNA section are some ideas how they would end, vivisected, objects of experiments, their abillity to shapeshift rejected by drugs, chemicals and other things.<br /> <br /> Lupus are sometimes abandoned after first change. Not everyone are found by garou. Some of them are lost, rejected by family pack.<br /> <br /> Metis sometimes have better start in matter of understanding who he is. Often their parents are to blame, not everyone treat metis as punchbag. Children of Gaia and Furies care about them, childrens of Unicorn look at them as equals.<br /> <br /> As I remember Fianna hate them the most, but overall revised tribebooks improved their position. Shadow Lords (one of the most ruthless garou) accepted them and granted with important tasks - Lazarite movement.<br /> <br /> Shame that creators see only one side of the coin - uncomfortable player character, offending to players and similar ideas, but not - interesting character, a character with a goal and soul, more difficult to play but more satisfying. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T05:31:43-07:00","id":1464013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464008#post1464008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say it is more making sure those who are disabled not having to deal with ableism during their fun time. I'm disabled and I like playing crinos-born, but I also have not been subjected to abuse over my disability.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, the inspirations for the breed are Quasimodo, Basket Case, Bat Boy from the Goonies, etc. Someone physically malformed who is an outsider and bitter about it. That 'deformed freak in the attic' trope is no longer something tolerated.<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> once noted that a metis character could also make other players uncomfortable, as they did not want to heap on abuse to a disabled person.<br /> <br /> Basically, I don't feel it is babyproofing as much as just addressing something that was once okay but no longer is because we are more aware of having disabled players around.<br /> <br /> Mind, I rather not have the breed removed, but I understand why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Naturallt, we can all agree that discrimination against the disabled is absolutely unnaceptable but at the same time we should acknowledge that the Garou Nation is not a particularly pleasant society to be born to. They are an hidebound people with archaic notions about things humans take for granted like sexual freedom. Even the most privileged members of this society are likely to end their days with a fomori's claws in their guts.<br /> <br /> We shouldn't glorify the Garou Nation but if we remove everything that can be unconfortable about it, we are gutting a good portion of the setting and removing fodder for stories. If everything that culturally makes the Garou the Garou, are they all that different from werewolves from a supernatural teen drama?<br /> <br /> For instance, obviously no one believes that it's good and proper for Silver Fang kinfolk to have arranged marriages so as to protect their purity and increase the chances of producing more Garou. But that makes for good stories.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T06:13:45-07:00","id":1464020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464013#post1464013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We shouldn't glorify the Garou Nation but if we remove everything that can be unconfortable about it, we are gutting a good portion of the setting and removing fodder for stories. If everything that culturally makes the Garou the Garou, are they all that different from werewolves from a supernatural teen drama?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing; Is the setting's cohesion more important than making sure a player in your group is not going to have flashbacks to their IRL abuse? I think the player's comfort is more important than being 1:1 with the book.<br /> <br /> Different people have different limits, and removing crinos-born is making sure a very common source of trauma is avoided.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T06:25:28-07:00","id":1464021,"title":"","content":"This drivel about Gaia and the Apocalypse sounds like something straight out of Black Spiral Dancer propaganda. Looks like I'm skipping this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","name":"Karthak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T06:27:08-07:00","id":1464022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464020#post1464020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's the thing; Is the setting's cohesion more important than making sure a player in your group is not going to have flashbacks to their IRL abuse? I think the player's comfort is more important than being 1:1 with the book.<br /> <br /> Different people have different limits, and removing crinos-born is making sure a very common source of trauma is avoided.</div> </div> </div> </div>A player's comfort should always take priority within the context of that group. But Werewolf: The Apocalypse is not meant for just one group. How much darknes are we willing to remove from the &quot;World of Darkness&quot; before all we are left with are surface elements? Any children's cartoon can tell us how pollution is bad.<br /> <br /> And it's not just about cohesion but quality. Judging by this particular interview, a great number of the core concept and themes of Werewolf are being axed including, but not limited to, the relationship between Tribe, Garou, Ancestors and the Spirit World itself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T06:36:35-07:00","id":1464024,"title":"","content":"see it's <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">alre</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">ady beginning, we're </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">alre</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">ady seeing divides on decisions </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">as niche </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">as i</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">ncest baby bullying m</span></span></span>aking it okay to sanitise a major plot point <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. Give it a year </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">and the split will be incredably bitter.....</span></span></span>again.<br /> <br /> Then again I'm okay with the metis tabboo thing because it discourages furry fetish shit so maybe I'm guilty of niche thinking as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-15-2021, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T06:50:50-07:00","id":1464025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464022#post1464022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A player's comfort should always take priority within the context of that group. But Werewolf: The Apocalypse is not meant for just one group. How much darknes are we willing to remove from the &quot;World of Darkness&quot; before all we are left with are surface elements? Any children's cartoon can tell us how pollution is bad.<br /> <br /> And it's not just about cohesion but quality. Judging by this particular interview, a great number of the core concept and themes of Werewolf are being axed including, but not limited to, the relationship between Tribe, Garou, Ancestors and the Spirit World itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, this is one darkness I can accept going. However, I do agree with others that there ARE some very bad choices present, even in the no-crinos-born idea. For one, BSDs losing basically the one thing that kept their numbers (somewhat) at check.<br /> <br /> And the VERY likely loss of lupus. If crinos-born are an issue, I've seen far more people throw HUGE fits over the very existence of lupus.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'm NOT okay with taking so much of the setting away. Its just that crinos-born are something I could see changed for a good reason.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T07:04:05-07:00","id":1464026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464025#post1464025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, this is one darkness I can accept going. However, I do agree with others that there ARE some very bad choices present, even in the no-crinos-born idea. For one, BSDs losing basically the one thing that kept their numbers (somewhat) at check.<br /> <br /> And the VERY likely loss of lupus. If crinos-born are an issue, I've seen far more people throw HUGE fits over the very existence of lupus.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'm NOT okay with taking so much of the setting away. Its just that crinos-born are something I could see changed for a good reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair. Personally, I'm not fond of it and see it as evidence of a general sanitization of the setting.<br /> <br /> Couldn't we just have Anarch Werewolves who have forsaken the Litany instead of rewriting Garou biology which seems to be what's implied by the absence of both Metis and the removal of the &quot;Garou shall not mate with Garou&quot; tenet from the Litany?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T07:07:41-07:00","id":1464027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464026#post1464026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't we just have Anarch Werewolves who have forsaken the Litany instead of rewriting Garou biology which seems to be what's implied by the absence of both Metis and the removal of the &quot;Garou shall not mate with Garou&quot; tenet from the Litany?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd LOVE if there was a more active ronin faction/factions. Because that would fit the setting and give players who don't want to play the Garou Nation something to do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T07:26:57-07:00","id":1464028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1463914#post1463914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll add something different:<br /> <br /> Going way back to when the nWW team was talking about their future plans, a bunch of us felt that what they really wanted to make was the CofD, but they wanted the brand recognition of the WoD. Martin basically admitted as much.<br /> <br /> V5 haphazardly grabbed from VtR, and some other games, and tried to smash it all together with VtM. I tried to wait and see. The playtests kept demonstrating that they weren't going to make the balancing act work in a fashion I'd like. Then V5 dropped and confirmed it. And then the V5 supplements continued to disappoint.<br /> <br /> W5 seems to repeating all of the same mistakes. Instead of trying to make a WtA for the 2020s, they're grabbing from Forsaken, and the BNS MET WtA book, and the I-already-don't-like-it V5. So what reason do I have to believe W5 is going to fix any of the development processes that created the V5 I don't want?<br /> <br /> What was announced that will actually appeal to me when I can play Forsaken or W20 instead?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Correction: Bits of Forsaken that Forsaken is moving away from.<br /> <br /> A werewolf plus a werewolf in 2E is a guaranteed wolfblood, nothing more or less, spirits may resent being disallowed into the mortal world but they recognize balance is generally better for most of them and they scurry out of the way when the Uratha are trying to get rid of a Wound, and while they generally stick to their own beats they happily coordinate with others if they realize it's a bigger problem than the pack's territory.<br /> <br /> So this comes off as a grognard for CofD 1E writing CWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T07:48:39-07:00","id":1464030,"title":"","content":"I think the multicultral things about tribes could be interesting.<br /> A pack of siberian fianna worshipping Stag in form of an Elk god of the hunt.<br /> A pack of wendigo on the forzen peaks of the alps worshipping the Wildman as Wendigo.<br /> A commando of Fenris from kazakhstan invoking the Tanri in his form of Wolf , like their brethren in scandinavia do with Fenris.<br /> <br /> Could be interesting to see how various players can see the tribes more as concept than ethno-cultural sects.<br /> I suppose the tribes definitely will get nicknames.<br /> <br /> But a part of me knows that all of this comes from Forsaken, and it makes me a little bit sad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T08:02:12-07:00","id":1464032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464022#post1464022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A player's comfort should always take priority within the context of that group. But Werewolf: The Apocalypse is not meant for just one group. How much darknes are we willing to remove from the &quot;World of Darkness&quot; before all we are left with are surface elements? Any children's cartoon can tell us how pollution is bad.<br /> <br /> And it's not just about cohesion but quality. Judging by this particular interview, a great number of the core concept and themes of Werewolf are being axed including, but not limited to, the relationship between Tribe, Garou, Ancestors and the Spirit World itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree with this. It seems like everyone except for the folks at Onyx Path don't seem to understand the World of Darkness and are either turn it into the World of Slight Twilight or Chronicles of Darkness: World of Darkness Edition.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness was always meant to be a darker, worse version of our world. None of the factions we play in are meant to be Paragons of Virtue but flawed institutions that often times are as much a cause of their problems as outside forces are. Yet often times we want to fight for these flawed institutions, to correct their flaws and show them a better way of doing things because despite their flaws these institutions call to us in their own ways.<br /> <br /> Yeah, there's a lot of problems with the Garou Nation but that's part of the point. Many of the Garou's problems were born out of their own mistakes, flaws and failings. Trying to just toss out some of those flaws is potentially detrimental to the line and it's themes.<br /> <br /> Between the recent W5 and H5 news as well as the stuff coming out about Bloodlines 2, I've lost much of my faith WoD products not being handled by OPP. And I think the most frustrating is that it feels like people running the brand aren't listening to us. It feels like we're screaming at the wind and if we're lucky one or two things we're yelling might be heard and they <i>might </i>consider what we've said. It's so frustrating and disheartening.<br /> <br /> Honestly at this point I don't expect to be buying 5E products unless they're OPP products or addons from OPP Kickstarters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T08:28:34-07:00","id":1464035,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that a constant pressure to modify everything into the context of period American insectionalist criteria is not only going be incredibly difficult to produce and still be compelling with broad appeal but is probably going to result in increasingly drastic backslashes at not only contested points of intersectional praxis but also out of raw frustration and exasperation at attempting to have fun in a hyper sanitised way with a layer of strong social ettitequte on top?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-15-2021, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T09:43:05-07:00","id":1464045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464035#post1464035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that a constant pressure to modify everything into the context of period American insectionalist criteria is not only going be incredibly difficult to produce and still be compelling with broad appeal but is probably going to result in increasingly drastic backslashes at not only contested points of intersectional praxis but also out of raw frustration and exasperation at attempting to have fun in a hyper sanitised way with a layer of strong social ettitequte on top?</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of miss the old 1st and 2nd edition days of free creativity and gonzo craziness. Sure, there were plenty of silly things that came out then, including historical or cultural inaccuracies, inconsistencies, or insulting stereotypes - but a lot of cool stuff came out then. The bad stuff could easily be discarded, or included if you like it, and we all know that geeks love having things to complain about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464026#post1464026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fair. Personally, I'm not fond of it and see it as evidence of a general sanitization of the setting.<br /> <br /> Couldn't we just have Anarch Werewolves who have forsaken the Litany instead of rewriting Garou biology which seems to be what's implied by the absence of both Metis and the removal of the &quot;Garou shall not mate with Garou&quot; tenet from the Litany?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some kind of &quot;Anarch&quot; movement within the Garou nation sounds like a great idea to me. Instead of making every Garou faction super woke and &quot;tolerant&quot; it would be far better to acknowledge how incredibly intolerant and rigid Garou society is and to emphasize that in combination with a focus on a younger generation of Garou who want to want to resist the hyper-conservative elders.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T09:43:26-07:00","id":1464046,"title":"","content":"Onyx Path upcoming Apocalyptic records have brilliant ideas so far, like AkatsukiLeder13 wrote fanbase ideas are unfamiliar to W5 designers. So far I enjoy W20 line very much. And so my ecpectations for W5 are.maby too high compered to OPP stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T11:11:38-07:00","id":1464058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464045#post1464045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kind of miss the old 1st and 2nd edition days of free creativity and gonzo craziness. Sure, there were plenty of silly things that came out then, including historical or cultural inaccuracies, inconsistencies, or insulting stereotypes - but a lot of cool stuff came out then. The bad stuff could easily be discarded, or included if you like it, and we all know that geeks love having things to complain about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Some kind of &quot;Anarch&quot; movement within the Garou nation sounds like a great idea to me. Instead of making every Garou faction super woke and &quot;tolerant&quot; it would be far better to acknowledge how incredibly intolerant and rigid Garou society is and to emphasize that in combination with a focus on a younger generation of Garou who want to want to resist the hyper-conservative elders.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Theirs something to be said of mad bastard game design, I mean phils made career out it. A lot of the more compelling settings are a product of thinking outside the box rather than carefully considered game design. It's arguable wod itself if a product of that in the context of the early 90s. I doubt you could make something as edgy and devil may care now. Although that's partly due to the sheer range now.<br /> <br /> You could make an anarch faction but I'd be very careful how you proceed. For a start I'd avoid simply poisoning the well with the garou nation like they did with the Sabbat or the carmarilla. You also need some productive differences in how they run things as well as some actual flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-15-2021, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T11:25:52-07:00","id":1464062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464046#post1464046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Onyx Path upcoming Apocalyptic records have brilliant ideas so far, like AkatsukiLeder13 wrote fanbase ideas are unfamiliar to W5 designers. So far I enjoy W20 line very much. And so my ecpectations for W5 are.maby too high compered to OPP stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>The people writing Apocalyptic Records aren't the same writing W5?<br /> How does that work?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23725-hardestadttheevenyounger","name":"HardestadtTheEvenYounger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23725_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T12:45:18-07:00","id":1464069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464062#post1464062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The people writing Apocalyptic Records aren't the same writing W5?<br /> How does that work?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Apocalyptic Record is the last of the Werewolf 20th Anniversary line, offering a sum up that is developed, guided, and written by Onyx Path veterans and newer writers alike.<br /> <br /> Werewolf the Apocalypse 5th edition is being done by Paradox Interactive, I've not been looking into it but I have no idea who's writing it. It's not Onyx Path. Similar to Vampire the Masquerade 5th edition it may just ignore the 20th Anniversary stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-15-2021, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T14:13:33-07:00","id":1464085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464020#post1464020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Here's the thing; Is the setting's cohesion more important than making sure a player in your group is not going to have flashbacks to their IRL abuse? I think the player's comfort is more important than being 1:1 with the book.<br /> <br /> Different people have different limits, and removing crinos-born is making sure a very common source of trauma is avoided.</div> </div> </div> </div>Abuse is a theme of this game. Kinfolk are abused by spouses. Cubs by power-drunken mentors. Bone Gnawers by everyone. Human children are thorn into bloody chunks by Red Talons. I could go ad nauseum...<br /> Physical agression is common as Garou are warriors spoiling for a fight. They systematicaly killed their own brothers (Fera &amp; Bunyip) and drove themeselves to near extinction.<br /> <br /> I think this game and background are not for anyone, but some people are looking for this darkness to fight it. It can be (again, not for everyone) therapeutic to face their own traumas in the games' paralels. For others it just causes damage. Game table can be a safe space to look deep into our own flaws and traumas and try to cope with them next to friends. It can also hurt.<br /> <br /> But sanitising this game, chipping away it's cores is just sad. In this setting the flaws were, for our group, merits. We were heroes fighting for the near-dead ideals, justice, acceptance, love, or just bite fomors into bits (pun intended). <br /> Taking away an injustice just take away a reason for a good fight and the chance of heroism.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T15:12:08-07:00","id":1464091,"title":"","content":"If all of the playable tribes are in the core book, then W5 has one leg up on V5, I suppose. It sounds like that's about all it has going for it. I've never been a passionate fan of Werewolf, and none of the changes cited have me saying, &quot;yes, now I'll play it, this is what I was waiting for.&quot; I have no idea who the target audience for this is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T15:21:39-07:00","id":1464093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464085#post1464085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Abuse is a theme of this game. Kinfolk are abused by spouses. Cubs by power-drunken mentors. Bone Gnawers by everyone. Human children are thorn into bloody chunks by Red Talons. I could go ad nauseum...<br /> Physical agression is common as Garou are warriors spoiling for a fight. They systematicaly killed their own brothers (Fera &amp; Bunyip) and drove themeselves to near extinction.<br /> <br /> I think this game and background are not for anyone, but some people are looking for this darkness to fight it. It can be (again, not for everyone) therapeutic to face their own traumas in the games' paralels. For others it just causes damage. Game table can be a safe space to look deep into our own flaws and traumas and try to cope with them next to friends. It can also hurt.<br /> <br /> But sanitising this game, chipping away it's cores is just sad. In this setting the flaws were, for our group, merits. We were heroes fighting for the near-dead ideals, justice, acceptance, love, or just bite fomors into bits (pun intended).<br /> Taking away an injustice just take away a reason for a good fight and the chance of heroism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One my proudest <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">achievements in g</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">ame w</span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">as pushing through </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">a minor reforms to protect kinfolk from </span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">abusive spouses (slightly).</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T17:19:25-07:00","id":1464108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464091#post1464091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If all of the playable tribes are in the core book, then W5 has one leg up on V5, I suppose. It sounds like that's about all it has going for it. I've never been a passionate fan of Werewolf, and none of the changes cited have me saying, &quot;yes, now I'll play it, this is what I was waiting for.&quot; I have no idea who the target audience for this is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, not all of them are. 11 is not the full count of Tribes and thats whats in W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T17:23:41-07:00","id":1464109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464062#post1464062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The people writing Apocalyptic Records aren't the same writing W5?<br /> How does that work?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Based on word from some of the writers ( who will remain nameless, cos they're awesome and PDX is vindictive) I correspond with, Paradoxs feedback on WtA books both W5 and W20 was basically ' make it edgier, lean more into outdated stereotypes, remove options, hope and nuance'.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T23:30:46-07:00","id":1464158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464062#post1464062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The people writing Apocalyptic Records aren't the same writing W5?<br /> How does that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Different projects, different companies, different game lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T04:04:27-07:00","id":1464171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardestadtTheEvenYounger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464062#post1464062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The people writing Apocalyptic Records aren't the same writing W5?<br /> How does that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple. Onyx Path are not connected to Paradox or the &quot;New White Wolf&quot;. They are simply licensees. They can pitch what they want to make, but Paradox decides what will get made or not. Paradox can also request changes, usually these don't seem too bad, but some books are reputed to have had a complicated process of being made (i.e. Changing Ways)<br /> <br /> When Paradox got the IP they made their own team of writers (originally lead by Erikson and now by Achilli) to make Vampire 5. This was a hand picked crew that was supposed to create the game and control where the setting goes, and they didn't really care what Onyx Path is doing. What they did do is conclude that they cannot publish these games, so they outsourced first to Modiphius and now to Hunters entertainment. They also concluded that while they can keep the direction an the main books to themselves, they can actually outsource the other books to anyone else - which is how OP got Chicago by Night, Modiphius Fall of London and Renegade Second Inqusition.<br /> <br /> For Werewolf they started with hunters/renegade as people who will make them for them, but they decided to abandon that and again went with internal group that will be making the new game an just leave it to hunters to publish. Further supplements will again likely be farmed out in any way they see fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T07:12:14-07:00","id":1464192,"title":"","content":"I'm seeing a lot of people concerned about taking elements from Forsaken and I think thats exactly what they are doing. I'm less bothered by that then many others seem to be but I think its pretty clear that's the direction the whole line is taking. the WoD20 line was a line that extended the history of the OWoD into a new era and has done so very well. that's not what WoD5 is doing. Starting with V5 its clear that the new line is intended less as a continuation of WoD20 with cleaned up mechanics and more as a comic book style post crisis multiversal merging of what the developers think are the best elements of both lines (while also cutting what they think are the worst elements). They are also clearly doing what both the NWod line and Mage Revised were doing which is to bring the play back to a more &quot;Street&quot; level and sweep away many of the elements that made players feel they lacked agency like extensive metaplot and incredibly powerful supernaturals that really run the show. And I think they are doing this because, while they would like for the older players to come along and be part of this, they really are aiming at new players with new sensibilities. If you love all the history and nostalgia of over 20 years of WoD then the 20th anniversary line already has everything we could possibly hope for. This new line is clearly aimed at newer players that need a different approach to gaming and world building and the developers are not being shy about how much they are picking a bit from column a and a bit from column B in mixing and matching from the two game lines to do so. Personally I'm OK with that even if i end up not playing the games. I actually like the V5 mechanics best of all three lines (OWoD/CoD and WoD5) so i'm mostly planning to take the new rules and adapt the story as i like to fir my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T07:32:45-07:00","id":1464193,"title":"","content":"I think the problem here is that while they may be making new experiences for new times they're not really approaching it in a way to rebuild it from the ground up. They are making the games they want to make based on their preferences and introducing &quot;one true way&quot; of how the games should be played. We saw how that ended up with Mage Revised.They could have gone and made things more flexible and open ended, even giving support to old playstyles and other ideas. I got no idea about the actual numbers of V5 sales beyond the intial buzz and the international drama, but the icv2 sales charts didn't really look encouraging.<br /> <br /> One of the best things that D&amp;D 5 did was to make it something where the setting and playstyle are malleable and open ended, and where you could equally run the modern modules or just something from old Planescape or Dark Sun if you felt like it. It might not be the best system to play fantasy, but it's got brand recognition, loads of support and allows a gamut of play styles to be used with it.<br /> <br /> Contrast this with V5 - if you don't want to play an Anarch, you're having bad wrong fun. If you want to be the Sabbat, tough. If you see Camarilla as the sensible option, tough, you're a fascist. Its designed to appeal to a certain type of players and without much care for the broader public. And honestly if they want the new WoD to be more than just a minor niche these games should be for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 10-16-2021, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T08:27:45-07:00","id":1464198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464193#post1464193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem here is that while they may be making new experiences for new times they're not really approaching it in a way to rebuild it from the ground up. They are making the games they want to make based on their preferences and introducing &quot;one true way&quot; of how the games should be played. We saw how that ended up with Mage Revised.They could have gone and made things more flexible and open ended, even giving support to old playstyles and other ideas. I got no idea about the actual numbers of V5 sales beyond the intial buzz and the international drama, but the icv2 sales charts didn't really look encouraging.<br /> <br /> One of the best things that D&amp;D 5 did was to make it something where the setting and playstyle are malleable and open ended, and where you could equally run the modern modules or just something from old Planescape or Dark Sun if you felt like it. It might not be the best system to play fantasy, but it's got brand recognition, loads of support and allows a gamut of play styles to be used with it.<br /> <br /> Contrast this with V5 - if you don't want to play an Anarch, you're having bad wrong fun. If you want to be the Sabbat, tough. If you see Camarilla as the sensible option, tough, you're a fascist. Its designed to appeal to a certain type of players and without much care for the broader public. And honestly if they want the new WoD to be more than just a minor niche these games should be for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never mind that CofD still exists and still has books published for it. Even without the setting change issues, is it wise to make one game so similar to another? When WtF was published, WtA was over. When W20 was released, WtF had already built itself an identity and a fanbase of its own.<br /> <br /> W5 is taking aspects of Forsaken that make it stand from WtA. This is an issue, because the uratha already share auspices and forms with the garou, with minor differences.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T09:16:26-07:00","id":1464201,"title":"","content":"Honestly after the ending of Werewolf the Apocalypse ( have Apocalypse book in my mind) they were immediately announcing new world of darkness, I'm a patient men so I waited for any news and one day they Announced Werewolf the Forsaken with five tribes. Immediately I've been comparing it to WtA, and thinning number of tribes was very strange. Some time later WtF was released and it was very very strange at first, but then I liked it more and more, with Hunters in the Darkness and Bone Shadows on the top. Denver was meaty and full of ideas and expanding the game with the Pures, Bale Hounds and Idigams convinced me that it's good game but different.<br /> Then W20 came and I gave all the books I had to my friend (all from 1 ed) for his birthday, cause old love never dies, and W20 line is very good in my opinion, it's like something you've lost and found it again and it made you happier then ever. Both games are about werewolves, spirit world and it's the biggest and maby the only one connection. Isn't W5 annunced similarities a theft of Forsasken fanbase or ideas? Maby it is? <br /> What's naive is that I belive that fanbase words are important for the game and writers.I know , very naive. I have no idea if the W5 writers listen to the fans or read forums. Maby some who have any contact with them should direct them to OPP forums? I expect that they have guidelines how W5 have to be, but I've met a lot people here smarter then me so please tell me, to whom is W5 adressed? <br /> From WOD site ,,Justin: \u201cW5 is an exciting project because I feel players will really connect with its content and message. So many people today are struggling with their frustrations about the climate crisis and what has become \u2018the new normal\u2019 and are unsure how to vent their anger. What better way than to cut loose as a Werewolf and hold those responsible accountable?\u201d.<br /> Do You people belive in that kind of thinking?&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T09:22:53-07:00","id":1464203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464201#post1464201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From WOD site ,,Justin: \u201cW5 is an exciting project because I feel players will really connect with its content and message. So many people today are struggling with their frustrations about the climate crisis and what has become \u2018the new normal\u2019 and are unsure how to vent their anger. What better way than to cut loose as a Werewolf and hold those responsible accountable?\u201d.<br /> Do You people belive in that kind of thinking?&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that is actually the reason why the tagline has always been &quot;When will you Rage.&quot; It is saying 'you see all this destruction and cruelty all around you and you feel angry about it. When will you let loose and Rage against all of it?' This theme has been in WtA from the start.<br /> <br /> This mentality is why WtA has such an interesting fanbase even with its flaws, it discusses things that are wrong in the world and lets you become a furry blender to avenge things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T09:32:25-07:00","id":1464205,"title":"","content":"I know but it's now what I'm asking for. ,,So many people today are struggling with their frustrations about the climate crisis and what has become \u2018the new normal\u2019 and are unsure how to vent their anger&quot;. So I wonder if WtA will include what's going on nowdays in the storyline, if yes how and why, and do You belive it would work. If the game is dark mirror of our world who might be behind pandemia (Pentex as always or Wyrm cults or Wyld immune system which is stupid in my opinion), Weaver vaccines as a defence from the pandemia ) ect. Should they mention it? Is the new economic crisis a important thing to use in WtA. - that is my apprehention..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 10-16-2021, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T10:12:08-07:00","id":1464206,"title":"","content":"W5 is going to be horrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T12:02:58-07:00","id":1464212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464058#post1464058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Theirs something to be said of mad bastard game design, I mean phils made career out it. A lot of the more compelling settings are a product of thinking outside the box rather than carefully considered game design. It's arguable wod itself if a product of that in the context of the early 90s. I doubt you could make something as edgy and devil may care now. Although that's partly due to the sheer range now.<br /> <br /> You could make an anarch faction but I'd be very careful how you proceed. For a start I'd avoid simply poisoning the well with the garou nation like they did with the Sabbat or the carmarilla. You also need some productive differences in how they run things as well as some actual flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, when the World of Darkness first came out, it was actually kind of subversive. Not quite as subversive as the authors probably thought, but it still had some controversial material in them that might have shocked or offended some people, that was outside of certain people\u2019s comfort zones, and that took a few risks.<br /> <br /> Now that is entirely the opposite. The WoD line is appealing to nostalgia of a 30 year old franchise, that is bending over backwards not to offend, that conforms to the ideology espoused by every powerful institution in the Western world. How can you be punk when those are the sensibilities that inform the creation of your setting?<br /> <br /> Anyway, when I say that I want Garou Anarchs, I don\u2019t want them in the same sense that Anarchs oppose the Camarilla in V:tM - especially not in V5. Rather I think it would be cool to have a movement within the Garou nation that socially opposed the rigidity, conservatism, and intolerance that largely defines Garou culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T09:36:02-07:00","id":1464260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464205#post1464205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know but it's now what I'm asking for. ,,So many people today are struggling with their frustrations about the climate crisis and what has become \u2018the new normal\u2019 and are unsure how to vent their anger&quot;. So I wonder if WtA will include what's going on nowdays in the storyline, if yes how and why, and do You belive it would work. If the game is dark mirror of our world who might be behind pandemia (Pentex as always or Wyrm cults or Wyld immune system which is stupid in my opinion), Weaver vaccines as a defence from the pandemia ) ect. Should they mention it? Is the new economic crisis a important thing to use in WtA. - that is my apprehention..</div> </div> </div> </div>WoD has typically kept their hands off most such events. The denizens of the WoD usually respond to them, rather than create them, so it's still fragmented habitats and bats, and the Triat isn't directly tapping its minions to do things that humans normally do in response, so while some organizations might have a hand in acquiring or distributing vaccines, they aren't making them or altering them in accordance with whatever conspiracy theory is being peddled on Facebook this week. I could also add that there aren't any drugs that cause Garou to stop being Garou (that was one of the lower moments of the otherwise good Subsidiaries book), as that would make the task of their enemies way too easy, and that silver nitrate hollow points were always a dumb idea, even if the W20 Book of the Wyrm started calling them poison rounds instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T09:55:40-07:00","id":1464262,"title":"","content":"If WtA was getting in on that, I'd say the best place is for Wyrm servants to be making the disinformation stuff worse for the double whammy of subverting the Weaver's fancy systems, and increasing human suffering. A couple of BSD kin in various social media bubbles stirring shit, some banes corrupting the pattern spiders that want a perfect algorithm, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T13:58:57-07:00","id":1464278,"title":"","content":"Just call Crinos-born something else and drop the disability angle. Then they stop being racist or ableist, but you can still keep the Breed. Flaws are already a thing if you want to play a disabled character.<br /> <br /> If you need to make a reason for the Crinos-born to be rare, just say that it's almost impossible for two Garou to get pregnant together. The magic just doesn't happen very often because reasons (Gaia likes to spread the love around, perhaps).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T02:22:52-07:00","id":1464339,"title":"","content":"I'm not even convinced getting rid of metis is a good thing rather than abelist. Their's a nasty subtext of shuffling people with a chronic established physiological disabilities out the room because they make others uncomfortable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-18-2021, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T03:42:13-07:00","id":1464349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464278#post1464278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just call Crinos-born something else and drop the disability angle. Then they stop being racist or ableist, but you can still keep the Breed. Flaws are already a thing if you want to play a disabled character.<br /> <br /> If you need to make a reason for the Crinos-born to be rare, just say that it's almost impossible for two Garou to get pregnant together. The magic just doesn't happen very often because reasons (Gaia likes to spread the love around, perhaps).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just keep the sterility angle and remove disability and the name. Because it is not the disability that is really the deal breaker for crinos-born. It is the sterility.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T05:25:50-07:00","id":1464363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464339#post1464339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even convinced getting rid of metis is a good thing rather than abelist. Their's a nasty subtext of shuffling people with a chronic established physiological disabilities out the room because they make others uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a line to balance here, certainly, but changing or removing the Garou-born doesn't, by itself, erase disabilities from the game. Retaining Flaws and the Battle Scar systems in some form ensures that Garou face disabilities as the story demands, while removing erasure's opposite bad extreme of bad reputation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464349#post1464349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or just keep the sterility angle and remove disability and the name. Because it is not the disability that is really the deal breaker for crinos-born. It is the sterility.</div> </div> </div> </div>By at least most medical definitions, sterility is a disability.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T05:54:42-07:00","id":1464368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464363#post1464363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a line to balance here, certainly, but changing or removing the Garou-born doesn't, by itself, erase disabilities from the game. Retaining Flaws and the Battle Scar systems in some form ensures that Garou face disabilities as the story demands, while removing erasure's opposite bad extreme of bad reputation.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> I think it does, erasing metis by writing already comes with the subtext that some forms of disability (inherited) are to be considered unseemly and the individuals suffering from it are an embarrassment to everyone else. Now we're just negotiating on what types of disability are ones we're you'd just prefer it if they didn't exist. Not in the &quot;you're condition is treated sense.&quot; But the &quot;I'd prefer not to be reminded of your presence even retroactively to the point I'm going to memory hole you.&quot;. <br /> <br /> Im naturally projecting my worst interpretation on this ill conceed and we don't actually know how they're removing the metis. but the more I think on this the less I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-18-2021, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T07:17:53-07:00","id":1464375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464205#post1464205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know but it's now what I'm asking for. ,,So many people today are struggling with their frustrations about the climate crisis and what has become \u2018the new normal\u2019 and are unsure how to vent their anger&quot;. So I wonder if WtA will include what's going on nowdays in the storyline, if yes how and why, and do You belive it would work. If the game is dark mirror of our world who might be behind pandemia (Pentex as always or Wyrm cults or Wyld immune system which is stupid in my opinion), Weaver vaccines as a defence from the pandemia ) ect. Should they mention it? Is the new economic crisis a important thing to use in WtA. - that is my apprehention..</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the pandemic is very topical, but honestly it's probably not that important of an issue to the Garou nation or even their enemies. The number of deaths and even the economic fallout is relatively small compared to the ever growing population of humans and their consumption habits, though if the human population were lowered slightly and/or the economy becomes a bit weaker and leads to less consumption and thus less environmental damage, then many werewolves would support that even if almost every human on Earth would not.<br /> <br /> If we go back to the conspiratorial material in the original WtA books and take that as inspiration, then Covid-19 was probably created by some kind of Wyrm agents and Pentex is manufacturing vaccines in order to put tainted substances into them. Of course, they aren't going to have that be the case in W5, if anything they are going to make antivax people Wyrm aligned. Really, I hope that they don't include anything about it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T07:31:51-07:00","id":1464378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464349#post1464349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or just keep the sterility angle and remove disability and the name. Because it is not the disability that is really the deal breaker for crinos-born. It is the sterility.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This.<br /> <br /> <br /> The &quot;Garou's need for humans to reproduce because they can't reproduce with each other&quot; is something important that doesn't deserve to be handwaved away with a shitty in-universe explanation.<br /> <br /> The kinfolk's reason for existing will lose most of its meaning. In a universe where garou can reproduce with each other, mating with humans poses more problems than it's worth. Delirium, Rage's scoring rule (if greater than the human's willpower causes panic), and simply living a double life between household obligations and Garou obligations sucks. Imagine Skyler and Walter (from breaking bad) arguing against each other. Now imagine a whole series of this. <i>Now</i> imagine a lifetime of this.<br /> Marrying another Garou makes things 100% easier. Far from perfect, but it would be at least a functional family, with no members passing out and developing literal PTSD every time someone goes to Crinos to kill the Fomori that invaded the backyard.<br /> <br /> Making a comparison, it would be as if V6 established that every vampire can create 1~5 blood humunculi, which are equal to human beings in intellect, appearance, physical abilities, and absolutely loyal. Suddenly, Ghouls' reason for existence loses much of its meaning.<br /> <br /> I don't think w5 will be for me. Not content with taking out Lupus, Get, Red Talons, Metis... and worse than it all, making the game more local, city level, street level (<i>blerg!</i>) like that other Werewolf rpg (since they are saying that the Garou nation is disunited &quot;because&quot;).<br /> <br /> <br /> On top of that, in my country the term used for Metis is something like &quot;Unclean (plural)&quot; so this is a problem for English language books only.<br /> <br /> An rpg where Metis and Lupus are not a thing already exists: WtF. If you want a werewolf rpg like that, feel free to migrate.<br /> <br /> Now, talking just about my personal opinion: The change in the litany sucks.<br /> <br /> It's pretty cool (not to say HOT) to have two characters who love each other, feel horny for each other, have a slow burn passion/sexual tension/love to finally fuck each other, but can't let anyone else discover their escapades. You know that part of the book that explains how to learn new Gifts? Which teacher and student go to a private place in the forest and train for days on end, and that such a process raise gossips because it was dangerous because such intimacy could often lead to both breaking the litany? Dude, that's hot lmao. Sad because in W5 the two will be able to fuck, get pregnant etc in front of everyone and no one will raise an eyebrow at that. Some things are only fun if they are prohibited. .<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, they're wasting a rich element of the setting. it has an interesting subtext to minority romance. I live in a country that's still fighting homophobia, with some married men in the closet, and so on. Something like Romeo and Juliet. I think the change will not make the rpg more receptive to minorities, but less. The idea of \u200b\u200bforbidden romance against the world will disappear because, suddenly, the majority of elders of the Garou Nation, with all their traditionalism, one day wake up and decide that left-wing social causes can step in and shape the rules of their Garou Nation. So sugary. So fluffy. So cute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","user":"blailton","date":". 10-18-2021, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T07:48:05-07:00","id":1464380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464368#post1464368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it does, erasing metis by writing already comes with the subtext that some forms of disability (inherited) are to be considered unseemly and the individuals suffering from it are an embarrassment to everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is more about a liability in the in-game universe. I mean &quot;Don't suffer thy people to tend your sickness&quot; and all that.<br /> <br /> Most player's I know are decent people and, I imagine, don't bully a person with a handicap. And they would welcome them to the game table, as do I. But as such, I would have a problem if I was required by the setting of the game to be a bully to a metis character, if the character was a PC. I can live with being an in-character jerk to an NPC as well as tolerate if NPCs are jerks to each other, and the ST describes such to trigger a reaction. Thing is, there is a difference between what I logically assume my characters stance would be, and what I am comfortable to play with. And I assume that is some aspect that many players have. Even more so in LARP.<br /> As such, I would be totally fine with removing metis from the PC options to make them NPCs only. Then again, some people might want to play the character who is treated badly, even more so, than the Bone Gnawers...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T12:26:27-07:00","id":1464403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464380#post1464380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is more about a liability in the in-game universe. I mean &amp;quot;Don't suffer thy people to tend your sickness&amp;quot; and all that.<br /> <br /> Most player's I know are decent people and, I imagine, don't bully a person with a handicap. And they would welcome them to the game table, as do I. But as such, I would have a problem if I was required by the setting of the game to be a bully to a metis character, if the character was a PC. I can live with being an in-character jerk to an NPC as well as tolerate if NPCs are jerks to each other, and the ST describes such to trigger a reaction. Thing is, there is a difference between what I logically assume my characters stance would be, and what I am comfortable to play with. And I assume that is some aspect that many players have. Even more so in LARP.<br /> As such, I would be totally fine with removing metis from the PC options to make them NPCs only. Then again, some people might want to play the character who is treated badly, even more so, than the Bone Gnawers...<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>By that logic couldn't you theoretically remove anything since someone somewhere might have strong personal feelings about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T13:22:05-07:00","id":1464413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464368#post1464368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it does, erasing metis by writing already comes with the subtext that some forms of disability (inherited) are to be considered unseemly and the individuals suffering from it are an embarrassment to everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so? I'm in a WtA game with someone who's playing a Homid Garou that's in a wheelchair due to a congenital disability. Getting rid of the Metis deformities wouldn't make inherited disabilities erased and thus have the subtext of making those disabilities unseemly. It would remove the divine-punishment angle of their deformities... which has the overt text of disabilities being unseemly and being an embarassament.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now we're just negotiating on what types of disability are ones we're you'd just prefer it if they didn't exist. </div> </div> </div>No. Now you're inventing this and inserting it into the conversation. Save your projecting of your worst interpretations for speculations about the game, not me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T14:13:48-07:00","id":1464418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464413#post1464413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How so? I'm in a WtA game with someone who's playing a Homid Garou that's in a wheelchair due to a congenital disability. Getting rid of the Metis deformities wouldn't make inherited disabilities erased and thus have the subtext of making those disabilities unseemly. It would remove the divine-punishment angle of their deformities... which has the overt text of disabilities being unseemly and being an embarassament.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No. Now you're inventing this and inserting it into the conversation. Save your projecting of your worst interpretations for speculations about the game, not me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well.....they've just erased a massive number of characters with inherited disabilities from the setting as well as that option in general. That's how they're directly removing a huge group with inherited disabilities. <br /> Plus the metis condition is through breeding/spirit issues not divine punishment. (I think, its been a while since I read that fluff).<br /> <br /> Possibly but considering they're gearing up to purge an entire group from the game it reflects pretty badly, I'm not even into angry call out antics online and think it looks bad.<br /> <br /> I will however conceed we don't actually know they're motivation yet. Should be interesting if we get an explanation or if its just they'd rather be making CoD WtF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-18-2021, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T15:43:39-07:00","id":1464425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464418#post1464418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well.....they've just erased a massive number of characters with inherited disabilities from the setting as well as that option in general. That's how they're directly removing a huge group with inherited disabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the Garou-born aren't good representations of disabilities. It's like complaining that a TV show cut 90% of the black characters from it, because they were all racist minstrel show caricatures before we even know if there's going to be increased black actors for new roles that aren't bad representation.<br /> <br /> You're also shifting the goal posts by moving from, &quot;cutting out the Garou-born cuts out inherited disabilities from the game,&quot; to &quot;cutting out the Garou-born cuts out a large number of characters with inherited disabilities from the game.&quot; We're not talking about what you first said about even a certain group of disabilities will even exist in the new game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus the metis condition is through breeding/spirit issues not divine punishment. (I think, its been a while since I read that fluff). </div> </div> </div>As I've pointed out in past threads in more exhaustive detail.<br /> <br /> 1) The Garou believe the Litany comes from Gaia. While there's evidence that the Litany is not a purely divine set of rules, as we know the Garou have added to it, Gaia and her loyal servants enforce the Litany, and empower punishment rites. If a Philodox performs a punishment rite successfully on two Garou that have had a child together, the spirits are giving their blessing to the Garou's belief that such actions deserved punishment for violating Gaia's laws.<br /> <br /> 2) The Garou do not have to have the specific breeding/spiritual issues presented. The rest of the Fera have a variety of ways in which mating among their own is handled. &quot;Deformed children as a punishment for their parents mating,&quot; is only a thing for the Garou and the Ratkin. Everyone else either: doesn't attach social stigma to it, considers their equivalent Breed better than those born to humans or animals, can't successfully mate with each other, or mating doesn't matter to making new members of their group (the Corax). The wider metaphysics of the setting don't bear out the idea that this is some incidental spiritual property of shifters. So either the Garou were made by their creators to be this way on purpose, or whatever spiritual process that so many other Fera have to avoid these things wasn't applied to the Garou for reasons.<br /> <br /> The Garou actively believe deformities are a divine punishment, and the setting gives a ton of evidence to back that belief up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Possibly but considering they're gearing up to purge an entire group from the game it reflects pretty badly, I'm not even into angry call out antics online and think it looks bad. </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is bad. Fixing the problems with the Garou-born is doable, and should be attempted before removing them.<br /> <br /> But trying to label the W5 creators as being ableists for cutting out ableist content is a big leap.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T16:00:19-07:00","id":1464427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464425#post1464425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaia and her loyal servants enforce the Litany, and empower punishment rites. If a Philodox performs a punishment rite successfully on two Garou that have had a child together, the spirits are giving their blessing to the Garou's belief that such actions deserved punishment for violating Gaia's laws</div> </div> </div> </div>One tiny nitpick, most of the punishment rites don't go into how just or deserved the punishment is, the spirits just do what they have agreed to do by the old agreements. Makes sense as most lower rank rites are enforced and affected by lesser spirits. Only the most extreme ones tend to have some loophole or where the Spirits actually perform some kind of assesment (and not even all of those). It's quite possible for a vengeful politically inclined Garou to manipulate people into punishing someone no matter how correct,deserved or just these punishments are.<br /> <br /> In general I'd say that a lot of these laws are the laws as presented and treated by the Garou rather then the laws as seen an interpreted by Gaia.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 10-18-2021, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T16:21:59-07:00","id":1464429,"title":"","content":"&quot;A failed rite is considered a sign from Gaia that the offending werewolf\u2019s crimes aren\u2019t significant to warrant such a punishment. Because these rites are enforced and empowered by the spirit world, truly unjust punishment rites may fail automatically, leading to a sure loss of Honor for the one who ordered them.&quot;<br /> <br /> - W20, page. 214<br /> <br /> As a default rule for all punishment rites, if the rite use isn't just, it may automatically fail. No need for individual loopholes in specific rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 10-18-2021, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T16:41:01-07:00","id":1464434,"title":"","content":"Same page: &quot;Truly unjust punishments <b>may</b> fail automaticaly&quot;<br /> <br /> Revised had &quot;At the Storyteller's discretion Punishment rites may fail automatically is the target is truly Innocent&quot;<br /> <br /> Neither of those excludes abuse. In my view how much the Spirits actually care about the Guilt of the target depends on how much Renown the target has and how big an injustice is being committed. I may be a bit cynical, but in my defense I'd see this as a rarity and an egregious sin against the Litany and the Garou, one when discovered would command the greatest of sanctions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T16:51:47-07:00","id":1464435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464425#post1464425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that the Garou-born aren't good representations of disabilities. It's like complaining that a TV show cut 90% of the black characters from it, because they were all racist minstrel show caricatures before we even know if there's going to be increased black actors for new roles that aren't bad representation.<br /> <br /> You're also shifting the goal posts by moving from, &quot;cutting out the Garou-born cuts out inherited disabilities from the game,&quot; to &quot;cutting out the Garou-born cuts out a large number of characters with inherited disabilities from the game.&quot; We're not talking about what you first said about even a certain group of disabilities will even exist in the new game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As I've pointed out in past threads in more exhaustive detail.<br /> <br /> 1) The Garou believe the Litany comes from Gaia. While there's evidence that the Litany is not a purely divine set of rules, as we know the Garou have added to it, Gaia and her loyal servants enforce the Litany, and empower punishment rites. If a Philodox performs a punishment rite successfully on two Garou that have had a child together, the spirits are giving their blessing to the Garou's belief that such actions deserved punishment for violating Gaia's laws.<br /> <br /> 2) The Garou do not have to have the specific breeding/spiritual issues presented. The rest of the Fera have a variety of ways in which mating among their own is handled. &quot;Deformed children as a punishment for their parents mating,&quot; is only a thing for the Garou and the Ratkin. Everyone else either: doesn't attach social stigma to it, considers their equivalent Breed better than those born to humans or animals, can't successfully mate with each other, or mating doesn't matter to making new members of their group (the Corax). The wider metaphysics of the setting don't bear out the idea that this is some incidental spiritual property of shifters. So either the Garou were made by their creators to be this way on purpose, or whatever spiritual process that so many other Fera have to avoid these things wasn't applied to the Garou for reasons.<br /> <br /> The Garou actively believe deformities are a divine punishment, and the setting gives a ton of evidence to back that belief up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, it is bad. Fixing the problems with the Garou-born is doable, and should be attempted before removing them.<br /> <br /> But trying to label the W5 creators as being ableists for cutting out ableist content is a big leap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct they're not a very good representation of IRL disabilities, but that's largely because garou arnt really human so metis are only a rough equivelant. It'd be more like cutting the klingons from star trek because the subtext you worried someone might make a fallacious comparison to irl cultures and then accidently implying something negative about martial irl cultures. then again star trek did have Black people planet and space irish so it's deeply context dependant. In this case I'd say no.<br /> <br /> I wouldnt really say I'm shifting the goalposts, it's more your reply is making me explore my casual observation deeper than my initial observation. The more we go into this the more dubious it looks. Also you misunderstood my initial point it isnt &quot;cutting out the Garou-born cuts out inherited disabilities from the game,&quot; it's: cutting out Metis implies a disabilities can intrisically disasteful and should be avoided in fiction. which is itself has nasty irl connetactions. that's more core comment.<br /> <br /> 1)That's a pretty good arguement but is more a reflection of umbral animaisim, i suppose it's a matter of perspective<br /> <br /> 2)on the other kind of disproves your point because the other Fera of it being divine are okay with it. Gaia's either playing favourates or something instrinsically goes wrong with metis.<br /> <br /> I disagree and it's worse to remove them so no it doesnt.<br /> <br /> Abelism is a strong word, truthfully I think they just want to make WTA more like WtF ala hunter and vtm and metis are very Apocalypse so they're going the way of Sabbat players or an nuanced approach the Carmarilla. Metis are probably pretty low on the problematic ranking compared to say...the Wendigo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-18-2021, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T17:41:43-07:00","id":1464437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464435#post1464435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct they're not a very good representation of IRL disabilities, but that's largely because garou arnt really human so metis are only a rough equivelant.</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels kinda weasel-word-ish.<br /> <br /> If comes off as if you're trying to say that because they're not good representation of disabilities, the offense people with disabilities have taken to how they're presented isn't important because the equivalence is too rough for it to count, but not so rough that cutting the Garou-born is anything but erasure.<br /> <br /> The Garou aren't &quot;really human,&quot; so what? Homids and lupus can have disabilities; including inherited ones. We don't need the Garou-born to represent disabilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it's: cutting out Metis implies a disabilities can intrisically disasteful and should be avoided in fiction. which is itself has nasty irl connetactions. that's more core comment. </div> </div> </div>And speaking of context, this doesn't address the context that we're dealing with a game that has it as a matter of fact in the setting that certain disabilities are intrinsically distasteful. How can cutting the Garou-born make the game's implications about disabilities worse than they already are? They're bad, and what you're talking about isn't a worse outcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I disagree and it's worse to remove them so no it doesnt. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you mean by this sentence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Abelism is a strong word,... </div> </div> </div>Sure, but you literally used it to describe cutting the Garou-born out of WtA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Metis are probably pretty low on the problematic ranking compared to say...the Wendigo. </div> </div> </div>It's not a contest that requires ranking.<br /> <br /> Also, they're cutting one, and keeping the other, which is more context to consider.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T18:13:03-07:00","id":1464438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An rpg where Metis and Lupus are not a thing already exists: WtF. If you want a werewolf rpg like that, feel free to migrate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, its been very clear to me since V5 that the nu-White Wolf writers and/or Paradox is heavily biased toward stuffing CofD into WoD/cWoD by any means necessary. All its doing is alienating the cWoD fanbase even more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T18:24:23-07:00","id":1464439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464437#post1464437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This feels kinda weasel-word-ish.<br /> <br /> If comes off as if you're trying to say that because they're not good representation of disabilities, the offense people with disabilities have taken to how they're presented isn't important because the equivalence is too rough for it to count, but not so rough that cutting the Garou-born is anything but erasure.<br /> <br /> The Garou aren't &quot;really human,&quot; so what? Homids and lupus can have disabilities; including inherited ones. We don't need the Garou-born to represent disabilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And speaking of context, this doesn't address the context that we're dealing with a game that has it as a matter of fact in the setting that certain disabilities are intrinsically distasteful. How can cutting the Garou-born make the game's implications about disabilities worse than they already are? They're bad, and what you're talking about isn't a worse outcome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you mean by this sentence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure, but you literally used it to describe cutting the Garou-born out of WtA.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's not a contest that requires ranking.<br /> <br /> Also, they're cutting one, and keeping the other, which is more context to consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry you feel that way but i think we can both agree that werewolves arnt a littteral comparison blow by blow of irl human disabilities right? Therefore were trying to argue they're a litteral equivelant doesnt really work right?<br /> <br /> I don't personally actually find the implications of them particulary offensive, you can argue divine punishment angle but I personally find it a pretty tepid arguement. ultimatly i find them implication of just whipping the board clean of disabled depictions because they make some people uncomfortable way worse even if i did conceed your perspective.<br /> <br /> Okay-simply put, no you're wrong.<br /> <br /> Yes upon consideration it was too strongly worded, I should have gone for problematic or something less severe. Good catch<br /> <br /> And?<br /> <br /> Is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T18:57:42-07:00","id":1464446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464439#post1464439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry you feel that way but i think we can both agree that werewolves arnt a littteral comparison blow by blow of irl human disabilities right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and neither of us claimed otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Therefore were trying to argue they're a litteral equivelant doesnt really work right? </div> </div> </div>Sure, but you're being extremely inconsistent in how you apply the figurative nature of the equivalence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ultimatly i find them implication of just whipping the board clean of disabled depictions because they make some people uncomfortable way worse even if i did conceed your perspective. </div> </div> </div>And here is the biggest issue regarding that inconsistency. You're arguing that taking out one element of the game, with a number of associations, is the same as removing <b>all people with disabilities from the game</b>.<br /> <br /> Do the rules disallow homids and lupus with disabilities? Are there no other ways to address people with disabilities in the game besides the Garou-born?<br /> <br /> Because you keep skipping this aspect of my responses to make what comes off as an exceedingly hyperbolic claim of &quot;implications.&quot;<br /> <br /> How about this? Doesn't cutting the Garou-born (or at least their connection to disability) actually make it easier to portray disabilities well in the game? One Breed so strongly defined by disabilities, but with many other strong issues attached to them, limits concepts the game can accomplish. Homid and lupus PCs with disabilities just come off as Garou-born PCs with players that don't want to have to deal with the rest of the Garou-born baggage; even in-character it creates an assumption that Garou with congenital disabilities are Garou-born unless proven otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay-simply put, no you're wrong. </div> </div> </div>About what? I'm not confused about the meaning of the words, I'm confused because it's not clear to me exactly which statements are meant to apply to what parts of what I said when they just stand alone. Am I wrong about everything? A specific point? Some evidence that may or may not make the totality of what I'm saying wrong?<br /> <br /> The same applies to these:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And?<br /> <br /> Is it? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T22:16:26-07:00","id":1464460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464349#post1464349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or just keep the sterility angle and remove disability and the name. Because it is not the disability that is really the deal breaker for crinos-born. It is the sterility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought that in-universe the reason that Gaia/The writers made Garou Born (I'm not going back! You can't make me!) sterile was because the Garou were such assholes that they'd do that as a way to breed a vast army of Garou with no ties to humanity or Lupus instead.<br /> <br /> Mind you, all my few Werewolf games emphasize the Garou as monsters who need human ties to avoid becoming horrible evil creatures. They are heroes but in the sense the Punisher and Wolverine are.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T23:50:54-07:00","id":1464468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464403#post1464403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By that logic couldn't you theoretically remove anything since someone somewhere might have strong personal feelings about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That is what makes the decision hard on what to put in the game and what to leave out. Every troupe I know house rules some part of the setting, handwaved it or the ST didn't touch it becuase he avoided it subconsiously or on purpose. It's just natural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T00:23:00-07:00","id":1464471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464339#post1464339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not even convinced getting rid of metis is a good thing rather than abelist. Their's a nasty subtext of shuffling people with a chronic established physiological disabilities out the room because they make others uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone with an invisible physical disability, I can assure you, the Crinos-born are unpleasant. Disability doesn't make someone evil, monstrous, cursed, etc. Nor is physical disability a curse for parents' bad behaviour. <br /> <br /> Yes, it's not real life, but as Heavy Arms pointed out, cutting out minstrels from your show is not racist against Black people. Putting them in is.<br /> <br /> You can introduce mystical curses all you want (something like Thin Blood Flaws for Crinos-born might be quite cool), but when you start adding in limb variance, hunchbacks, etc, it gets really unpleasant, really quickly.<br /> <br /> It's not about removing things that are uncomfortable for able-bodied players. It's about removing the fact that the main group of disabled Garou are objectively monstrous/cursed in the game, and what that means if you have a disability and want to play the game. I'm trying to centre the concerns of disabled people, not the able-bodied here, since this largely doesn't affect them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464368#post1464368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it does, erasing metis by writing already comes with the subtext that some forms of disability (inherited) are to be considered unseemly and the individuals suffering from it are an embarrassment to everyone else. Now we're just negotiating on what types of disability are ones we're you'd just prefer it if they didn't exist. Not in the &quot;you're condition is treated sense.&quot; But the &quot;I'd prefer not to be reminded of your presence even retroactively to the point I'm going to memory hole you.&quot;. <br /> <br /> Im naturally projecting my worst interpretation on this ill conceed and we don't actually know how they're removing the metis. but the more I think on this the less I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you genuinely believe all of this? Please don't tell me that keeping the Crinos-born in is somehow better for me. It's not. Trust me on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 10-19-2021, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T02:10:54-07:00","id":1464482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464471#post1464471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone with an invisible physical disability, I can assure you, the Crinos-born are unpleasant. Disability doesn't make someone evil, monstrous, cursed, etc. Nor is physical disability a curse for parents' bad behaviour.<br /> <br /> Yes, it's not real life, but as Heavy Arms pointed out, cutting out minstrels from your show is not racist against Black people. Putting them in is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I had epilepsy for the first 14 years of my life and am neuroatypical so I have some experience with disability. My wife is a Werewolf gamer and very much disabled. I thought it was always clear that the Crinos born were every bit as heroic as other Garou. Indeed, it was baked into the DNA that they suffered from discrimination and racism in-universe because the Garou Nation was, with two tribal exceptions, a bunch of assholes.<br /> <br /> Assholes who protected the Earth from annihilation but unless you were a Stargazer or Child of Gaia then you were some kind of dickbag.<br /> <br /> When were the Crinos Born ever people who deserved all the shit they were put through in-story? I thought the whole point was the whole &quot;Jon Snow is an outsider but a better guy in Westeros than anyone regardless of whether he's a bastard&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-19-2021, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T02:23:02-07:00","id":1464483,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Accusing the developers of erasure of disabled people [via removal of those created by mystic curse] is a strange charge to make.<br /> <br /> Also a reminder to keep all issues of posters to reports.<br /> <br /> I will keep an eye on this thread and let's hope it can remain civil.</span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-19-2021, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T02:38:33-07:00","id":1464488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464471#post1464471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone with an invisible physical disability, I can assure you, the Crinos-born are unpleasant. Disability doesn't make someone evil, monstrous, cursed, etc. Nor is physical disability a curse for parents' bad behaviour.<br /> <br /> Yes, it's not real life, but as Heavy Arms pointed out, cutting out minstrels from your show is not racist against Black people. Putting them in is.<br /> <br /> You can introduce mystical curses all you want (something like Thin Blood Flaws for Crinos-born might be quite cool), but when you start adding in limb variance, hunchbacks, etc, it gets really unpleasant, really quickly.<br /> <br /> It's not about removing things that are uncomfortable for able-bodied players. It's about removing the fact that the main group of disabled Garou are objectively monstrous/cursed in the game, and what that means if you have a disability and want to play the game. I'm trying to centre the concerns of disabled people, not the able-bodied here, since this largely doesn't affect them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Do you genuinely believe all of this, or are you just concern trolling? Don't tell me that keeping the Crinos-born in is somehow better for me. It's not. Trust me on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really didn't want to wheel this out but as someone who also has a invisible disability (one that was gentetically inherited) I have no problem with it. Its not a equivalent, the closest equivalent would be incest which is does produce health issues and is taboo,.but even that falls short since what we're discussing are supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> I don't really consider minstrels a valid comparison. They're nothing like metis in any context as I told Heavy Arms.<br /> <br /> Yes wod is a complex often uncomfortable setting exploring a large variety of difficult topics. Naturally I cannot decide what is or isn't okay for others on the table but wod has always been a game uncomfortable exploring issues which make people uncomfortable so I don't really consider it off limit.<br /> <br /> All garou are monstrous but I get your point. I can't speak for your lived experience of disability but you cannot speak for mine (frustrating and occasionally humiliating) or us as a collective. That you find them problematic is a valid perspective, i don't and find purging them has a disturbing subtext. In this were at an impasse. So we have to go to our own reasoning on the subject.<br /> <br /> <br /> I could imply the same for people who sincerely believe a race of fictional supernatural monsters inherated medical problems are a valid comparison to irl blackface. It isn't better for you, it isn't better for me. I'm a little critical of it even mattering irl. But I sincerely dislike the idea of sweeping an entire sub group under the rug because of a corporations/people on the internets interpretation of what's good taste as though disabilities are an issue of 'taste'.<br /> <br /> This is obviously going to turn into a big derail so I'm, going to try to avoid replying further unless something new comes up. Apologies everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-19-2021, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T05:14:21-07:00","id":1464505,"title":"","content":"Sorry, does 'minstrel' have a secondary meaning I don't catch? Because it translates to some mideval singer or musician in the online dictionary I looked it up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464482#post1464482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was always clear that the Crinos born were every bit as heroic as other Garou. Indeed, it was baked into the DNA that they suffered from discrimination and racism in-universe because the Garou Nation was, with two tribal exceptions, a bunch of assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not per definition. Those born of a forbidden union are, as you point out, <b>every bit as likely</b> to be heroes, so they are just as likly to become villains, or ronin, or mediocre garou as they are likely to become heroes.<br /> It isn't &quot;baked in their DNA&quot; that others discriminate against them. They don't have a pheromone that forces others to diminish them (although, that could be a deformity).<br /> <br /> But social dynamics, sterotyping, re-inforcing misconceptions, confirmation bias and peer pressure are real things too, and they work because that is how human brains work - and by extension the brains of garou. Succumbing to or falling in line with the society as a whole isn't something that makes a person an asshole, per s\u00e9. Some might be, but others don't realise the problem their behaviour creates or the serverity of it. Being uneducated in tha regard is a disatvantage in its own right, and being labled an asshole doesn't neccessarily encourage to rethink one's position...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T05:26:04-07:00","id":1464507,"title":"","content":"I'm quickly realising that we should move on from this particular topic, as people obviously have very strong opinions and aren't going to agree. <br /> <br /> For my part, I sometimes come across as more strident than I mean to be because I have ADHD (as well as other things) and it makes me, shall we say, intensely passionate about things in the moment (though less so when in time I am distracted and move onto something new) and sometimes quite blunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T05:29:10-07:00","id":1464508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464505#post1464505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, does 'minstrel' have a secondary meaning I don't catch? Because it translates to some mideval singer or musician in the online dictionary I looked it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a racist type of stage show where people dressed up as and parodied Black folk in a really awful way. It's generally regarded as pretty racist by most people. But, that's a whole other can of worms we shouldn't get into...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T07:40:09-07:00","id":1464511,"title":"","content":"Wikipedia pointed me to this <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minstrel_show\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minstrel_show</a><br /> <br /> Never heard of it before as minstrels are actually a historically relevant thing and not inherently tied to racisim in other parts of the world. Heck when Jethro Tull sings of the minstrel in the garden, or when AlanA-Dale plays the lute, they sure as hell aren't tied to racism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T08:10:09-07:00","id":1464514,"title":"","content":"So, I read the info paragraphs in the English and German wikipedia entry. Thanks for the link.<br /> As I see it, they are a cultural phenomenon and it would be kind of revisionism to say they didn't happen and ban them from a Werewolf Wild West Setting, for example.<br /> <br /> And what role they played in American culture as a whole is debatable. For example, the German version states that as these Ministrel shows continued to be popular, more and more elements of black culture were integrated and less distorted as in the beginning. Musicians who were actually black began performing and started their careers by playing Blues and Jazz music - exposing white Americans to this kind of music.<br /> On the other hand, the shows led to working class labourers projecting their problems on the slaves instead of connecting them with the changes in society and the work situation in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T09:54:26-07:00","id":1464519,"title":"","content":"Randon fact but one of the characters in a rare crossover game I did was the &quot;revelation&quot; (that was just one Garou's vision) was the First Ronin from the Book of the Wyrm who was the First Crinos Born was actually Caine after the Gurahl failed to bring him back.<br /> <br /> It was the werewolf &quot;origin&quot; myth for vampires.<br /> <br /> Which was another reason that they got shit on for &quot;ancestor guilt.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T09:55:28-07:00","id":1464520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464507#post1464507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm quickly realising that we should move on from this particular topic, as people obviously have very strong opinions and aren't going to agree.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Probably a good idea.</span></b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464514#post1464514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I read the info paragraphs in the English and German wikipedia entry. Thanks for the link.<br /> As I see it, they are a cultural phenomenon and it would be kind of revisionism to say they didn't happen and ban them from a Werewolf Wild West Setting, for example.<br /> <br /> And what role they played in American culture as a whole is debatable. For example, the German version states that as these Ministrel shows continued to be popular, more and more elements of black culture were integrated and less distorted as in the beginning. Musicians who were actually black began performing and started their careers by playing Blues and Jazz music - exposing white Americans to this kind of music.<br /> On the other hand, the shows led to working class labourers projecting their problems on the slaves instead of connecting them with the changes in society and the work situation in general.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Minstrel shows are considered highly racist by black Americans and usually were done by white men in blackface designed to denigrate African Americans.<br /> <br /> Please don't bring them up here.</span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-20-2021, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T19:35:44-07:00","id":1464553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464460#post1464460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always thought that in-universe the reason that Gaia/The writers made Garou Born (I'm not going back! You can't make me!) sterile was because the Garou were such assholes that they'd do that as a way to breed a vast army of Garou with no ties to humanity or Lupus instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they date back to the time before the Garou had done anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> 