the Garou blame the Crinosborn because theyr'e assholes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The books heavily disagree about superantihero comparisons, because of the elements of struggle and suffering and perseverance of the modern werewolves out to actually do their job. Also, wolf ties ought to be just as weighty in a game about how humans have put themselves on a pedestal that they do not deserve. </div> </div> </div>One would think wrestling with inner demons is part of WHY they are antiheroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T20:02:24-07:00","id":1464558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464555#post1464555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, if you want garou to keep ties to wolves and humans both you might want to punish them for mating with each other. However, as we know, the Garou blame the Crinosborn because theyr'e assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, the Nagah get to be interfertile with each other without cursebabies. Quite the opposite, in fact, though ahi only happen once per lifetime of the mother. And boy did the wereserpents fuck up... but they still get to have kids with each other.<br /> <br /> Garou would also probably be able to handle this. There would be a lot of politics involved, which would go a long way toward making sure that a notable portion of Garou don't get with other Garou. The other would be the danger inherent in having two high Rage killing machines shacking up and having to take care of kids that don't share their resilience or ferocity (the Nagah, incidentally, find it harder to develop high Rage).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One would think wrestling with inner demons is part of WHY they are antiheroes. </div> </div> </div>They... aren't supposed to be antiheroes? Like, the normal course of the game is to defeat the monster eating the heart of the world. There isn't an expectation that you'll backslide down a moral code and become what you're fighting, and you don't have to make compromises in order to stay functional like in Vampire, or at least, not the same kind of compromises. Nothing compels you to eat humans, and that's never really the intended result of a typical W:tA game - there's even a hard and fast rule about it in the code of conduct that everyone is expected to follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T01:44:32-07:00","id":1464570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464558#post1464558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They... aren't supposed to be antiheroes? Like, the normal course of the game is to defeat the monster eating the heart of the world. There isn't an expectation that you'll backslide down a moral code and become what you're fighting, and you don't have to make compromises in order to stay functional like in Vampire, or at least, not the same kind of compromises. Nothing compels you to eat humans, and that's never really the intended result of a typical W:tA game - there's even a hard and fast rule about it in the code of conduct that everyone is expected to follow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think superheroes are skewing people's vision of what Heroes are. Werewolves are Heroes in the classicist sense - great people doing great deeds with great burdens and flaws. Hercules and Theseus were doing good things, but that doesn't mean they were always good people. This is in stark contrast to the whole grimdark antihero trope.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T13:06:45-07:00","id":1464625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464555#post1464555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, if you want garou to keep ties to wolves and humans both you might want to punish them for mating with each other. However, as we know, the Garou blame the Crinosborn because theyr'e assholes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they?<br /> There is a legend in &quot;Guardians of the Caerns&quot; about the first Metis, it is not necessarily the first Ronin but clearly states the Law was in place before the baby was made and gives the War of Rage as a time frame.<br /> But the question is, what legends about the Crinosborn informed the generations and generations of garou that followed. Garou culture is oral for the most part. We know the Fianna are abrasive towards the crinos-born because they believe only in a healthy body can a healthy soul live. What events with crinos-born occurred to let such a doctrine emerge out of anecdotal evidence?<br /> <br /> Some crinos-born of pre-history might have screwed up in a big way or be blamed for some major shit so that the while species of garou leans toward abrasive stances against the crinos-born as a result. And of course, there might be a lot of self-fulfilling prophecy in that. Meaning a crinos-born being mistreated, therefore being more likely to turn towards the Wyrm, therefore causing more distrust and disgust towards all crinos-born... and so on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T13:19:02-07:00","id":1464630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464625#post1464625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they?<br /> There is a legend in &quot;Guardians of the Caerns&quot; about the first Metis, it is not necessarily the first Ronin but clearly states the Law was in place before the baby was made and gives the War of Rage as a time frame.<br /> But the question is, what legends about the Crinosborn informed the generations and generations of garou that followed. Garou culture is oral for the most part. We know the Fianna are abrasive towards the crinos-born because they believe only in a healthy body can a healthy soul live. What events with crinos-born occurred to let such a doctrine emerge out of anecdotal evidence?<br /> <br /> Some crinos-born of pre-history might have screwed up in a big way or be blamed for some major shit so that the while species of garou leans toward abrasive stances against the crinos-born as a result. And of course, there might be a lot of self-fulfilling prophecy in that. Meaning a crinos-born being mistreated, therefore being more likely to turn towards the Wyrm, therefore causing more distrust and disgust towards all crinos-born... and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel this falls into the trap that prejudice NEEDS a justification. The Garou hate the Crinosborn because the Garou are elitist bigots. This is an element that was there from the 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> One of the things about Pure Breed (and why it lacks now) was that it gave a lot of Garou a lot of unearned privilege.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464558#post1464558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They... aren't supposed to be antiheroes? Like, the normal course of the game is to defeat the monster eating the heart of the world. There isn't an expectation that you'll backslide down a moral code and become what you're fighting, and you don't have to make compromises in order to stay functional like in Vampire, or at least, not the same kind of compromises. Nothing compels you to eat humans, and that's never really the intended result of a typical W:tA game - there's even a hard and fast rule about it in the code of conduct that everyone is expected to follow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean there is the assumption you will accidentally kill some innocent people along the way, probably a lot of them. Werewolves are like Solar Exalted in the sense that yes, they are heroes and can save the world but may end up murdering their families like Herakles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T15:09:04-07:00","id":1464644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464630#post1464630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel this falls into the trap that prejudice NEEDS a justification. The Garou hate the Crinosborn because the Garou are elitist bigots. This is an element that was there from the 1st Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I can't accept that a whole species is hateful towards the Crinosborn without an explanation. Be it historical or evolutionary or supernatural or what ever.<br /> <br /> But, I'm also one of the people who found Heaths Ledger's Joker portraial not that groundbreaking and thought &quot;Some people just want to see the world burn&quot; a less than satisfying character motivation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464630#post1464630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things about Pure Breed (and why it lacks now) was that it gave a lot of Garou a lot of unearned privilege.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also disagree, and think that Pure Breed, as Ethan Skemp detailed once in the White Wolf forums, was misunderstood even by some authors.<br /> <br /> Point is, if a character has pure breed, he or she is closer to the ideals of his or her given tribe. This, in the typical nature vs. nurture question, would mean that the character in any case would have not only the disposition to be a remarkable garou (within his or her tribals standards) but also the inner drive and yearning to do so.<br /> A Silver Fang would never be a sluggard (Harano not withstanding).<br /> <br /> The problem is, that players and some authors alike saw the trait as a cheap way to social roll bonus dice. And over several iterations of the rules the concept of pure breed was changed bit by bit, for even the authors didn't understand how it was supposed to work (according to Ethan, which is the way it first made real sense to me).<br /> <br /> In our LARP, we (the STs) strip people of their pure breed trait, if they aren't able or at least make an effort, to convey that they are archetypical to their chosen tribe and by extension exemplary Garou in general.<br /> <br /> It is my believe, that having Pure Breed is a character trait that actually says something about the psyche of the garou, in more ways than being adored by others. And this drive and ambition might be misguided, like with the purest of his generation, Arkady.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T15:19:31-07:00","id":1464646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464644#post1464644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. I can't accept that a whole species is hateful towards the Crinosborn without an explanation. Be it historical or evolutionary or supernatural or what ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, bigots are motivated by no reason other than providing an outclass. The Crinosborn are the result of liasons forbidden by Gaia for whatever reason but they are hated for something completely not their fault and forced to go the extra mile for respect they deserve from people.<br /> <br /> But I'd be interested in why you think the Garou are bigoted against the Crinosborn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, I'm also one of the people who found Heaths Ledger's Joker portraial not that groundbreaking and thought &quot;Some people just want to see the world burn&quot; a less than satisfying character motivation.<br /> <br /> I also disagree, and think that Pure Breed, as Ethan Skemp detailed once in the White Wolf forums, was misunderstood even by some authors.<br /> <br /> Point is, if a character has pure breed, he or she is closer to the ideals of his or her given tribe. This, in the typical nature vs. nurture question, would mean that the character in any case would have not only the disposition to be a remarkable garou (within his or her tribals standards) but also the inner drive and yearning to do so.<br /> A Silver Fang would never be a sluggard (Harano not withstanding).<br /> <br /> The problem is, that players and some authors alike saw the trait as a cheap way to social roll bonus dice. And over several iterations of the rules the concept of pure breed was changed bit by bit, for even the authors didn't understand how it was supposed to work (according to Ethan, which is the way it first made real sense to me).<br /> <br /> In our LARP, we (the STs) strip people of their pure breed trait, if they aren't able or at least make an effort, to convey that they are archetypical to their chosen tribe and by extension exemplary Garou in general.<br /> <br /> It is my believe, that having Pure Breed is a character trait that actually says something about the psyche of the garou, in more ways than being adored by others. And this drive and ambition might be misguided, like with the purest of his generation, Arkady. </div> </div> </div>Except there have been many Pure Breed Garou who are complete bastards in the books as well as completely divorced from their tribes' expected behavior.<br /> <br /> My take on Pure Breed is it is purely a measure of how you look to other Garou and fitting their Platonic Idea of how a specific tribe should present themselves. It also is something that is a flaw in the Garou character as a ranting Silver Fang madman like Jacob Morningkill will always be followed over a cunning sensible Bone Gnawer.<br /> <br /> This is probably a matter of Storytellers emphasizing different things but the Garou Nation being at odds with itself was something that I felt was strongly emphasized by the original Storyteller's Handbook and I've always used that as a guide.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://encrypted-tbn3.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcQlon3A5UnN1NtAbOGXQUFYVmO6oIUoq3XXjh-WeDMWXT_zWg6Q\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T15:41:16-07:00","id":1464649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464630#post1464630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel this falls into the trap that prejudice NEEDS a justification. The Garou hate the Crinosborn because the Garou are elitist bigots. This is an element that was there from the 1st Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite. Prejudice and bigotry are irrational.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean there is the assumption you will accidentally kill some innocent people along the way, probably a lot of them. Werewolves are like Solar Exalted in the sense that yes, they are heroes and can save the world but may end up murdering their families like Herakles. </div> </div> </div>Yet the familymurder doesn't actually seem to happen very often in the setting a presented; when it does happen, it is an unusual tragedy (if only because the typical standard is that a werewolf lives apart from a mostly human family and isn't around nearly often enough to risk killing them by frenzy). Even the indiscriminate killing isn't really something that happens very much outside of some particularly traumatic First Changes or characters who are shown as being unhinged and potentially in the process of falling to the Wyrm; domination by a spirit (possession in any other game, but here that means something other than just being temporarily controlled) is sometimes also a cause, which isn't really the fault of the werewolf in question. It's the spirit, bane or otherwise, being a dick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T16:12:27-07:00","id":1464655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464646#post1464646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably a matter of Storytellers emphasizing different things but the Garou Nation being at odds with itself was something that I felt was strongly emphasized by the original Storyteller's Handbook and I've always used that as a guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do keep in mind that it's a book from 1994. I seem to remember it even having the conversion from 1E's thousands of renown to the modern system. And while it's loaded with cool stuff, WW has changed and fine tuned a lot after it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T16:28:31-07:00","id":1464658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464655#post1464655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do keep in mind that it's a book from 1994. I seem to remember it even having the conversion from 1E's thousands of renown to the modern system. And while it's loaded with cool stuff, WW has changed and fine tuned a lot after it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it depends then on how much you think it has changed and is no longer relevant.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T16:45:55-07:00","id":1464661,"title":"","content":"A lot. Garou were made more human and more diverse, and the reasons why they do things became a lot more nuanced than &quot;we're stuck up assholes&quot;. And I say this keeping in mind the essays to the back of the book and ST advice in that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T19:54:11-07:00","id":1464957,"title":"","content":"For now I'll give my two cents based only on pages 1 and 7 of this thread, I'll read the rest later.<br /> <br /> I personally think the Red Talons harm the game more than improve it, since always, so I'll be clear out of the bat that I do think they make sense as non Wyrm antagonists that don't follow the litany.<br /> <br /> Making any other tribe unplayable is bollocks, even when they threw the Stargazers in the Courts they kept them playable.<br /> <br /> Haglust is something I have to see before judging. The same for the new Renown mechanics. While Blood Potency wasn't the brightest idea in V5, I generally liked or was at least ok with the V5 mechanics.<br /> <br /> Apocalypse Yesterday and hostile Umbra are also somethings that I have to see first, but in lore their record is far less impressive, not to say impressively stupid. Lots of ok ideas with bad execution.<br /> <br /> Getting rid of Metis is just a big NO, more than anything else up to now. I don't care about the Watsonian explanation, it only harms many of the themes and play styles. As a disabled person myself I want to thank Paradox for genocide of disabled werewolves as a concept. Go fuck yourselves, I hate you.<br /> <br /> Pure Breed is a more complex matter, with many layers of pros and cons. In this regard, it is maybe for the best that they're not going to try. The point being that most interpretations people give to it are inherently true, the good and the bad.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, Garou are tragic heroes. As much as it means they have flaws, it is a very different trope from the antihero. The Garou society does have far more flaws itself than some players recognize, but it is not a society of pure assholes. They have lots of flaws, like many human societies, and frequently think they're entitled to their views, but those same views being challenged from within is equally a big part of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T20:44:06-07:00","id":1465469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464020#post1464020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's the thing; Is the setting's cohesion more important than making sure a player in your group is not going to have flashbacks to their IRL abuse? I think the player's comfort is more important than being 1:1 with the book.<br /> <br /> Different people have different limits, and removing crinos-born is making sure a very common source of trauma is avoided.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me it is (not going by the book, but by the darkest parts of my mind). I put all the s&amp;\u00a3t this world has to offer, let them grow in my head and than throw my players right into their faces. If someone can't hadle it that's ok, there are other storytellers. <br /> BUT<br /> I always ask my players before we start how far they want to go with me. They can draw the line. I will of course bend it to my will and imagination but never cross. But it's a one way ticket. Once the campaign is started there's no turning back (except leaving).<br /> Asking is easy. So when I read some of the creator's ideas and your interpretation of it it gives me a bitter taste in my mouth. I feel that someone thinks that me and my players are too dumb to play with some toys so they will take them away from us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T21:20:03-07:00","id":1465474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464471#post1464471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone with an invisible physical disability, I can assure you, the Crinos-born are unpleasant. Disability doesn't make someone evil, monstrous, cursed, etc. Nor is physical disability a curse for parents' bad behaviour. <br /> <br /> Yes, it's not real life, but as Heavy Arms pointed out, cutting out minstrels from your show is not racist against Black people. Putting them in is.<br /> <br /> You can introduce mystical curses all you want (something like Thin Blood Flaws for Crinos-born might be quite cool), but when you start adding in limb variance, hunchbacks, etc, it gets really unpleasant, really quickly.<br /> <br /> It's not about removing things that are uncomfortable for able-bodied players. It's about removing the fact that the main group of disabled Garou are objectively monstrous/cursed in the game, and what that means if you have a disability and want to play the game. I'm trying to centre the concerns of disabled people, not the able-bodied here, since this largely doesn't affect them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you think that Metis existence and the way they are treated are actually a finger pointed at anyone who mistreats disabled IRL (like albino hunters in Africa)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T22:24:22-07:00","id":1465478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465474#post1465474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't you think that Metis existence and the way they are treated are actually a finger pointed at anyone who mistreats disabled IRL (like albino hunters in Africa)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The killing of disabled people isn't exclusive to specific populations with poor education and specific superstitions. It happens in every nation at alarming rates, along with many other forms of mistreatment.<br /> <br /> Comparing the mistreatment of disabled people specifically with such a specific stance gives a wrong idea of the subject and is, in itself, offensive to the many victims that remain invisible in &quot;educated&quot; societies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T22:29:13-07:00","id":1465479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1464045#post1464045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some kind of &quot;Anarch&quot; movement within the Garou nation sounds like a great idea to me. Instead of making every Garou faction super woke and &quot;tolerant&quot; it would be far better to acknowledge how incredibly intolerant and rigid Garou society is and to emphasize that in combination with a focus on a younger generation of Garou who want to want to resist the hyper-conservative elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's strange is that early Werewolf very much plays up the fact that there is a rebellion brewing within the Garou Nation. Young Garou are either jaded about traditional Garou values because they clash with modernity, or they realize the old leadership is failing badly and need to be removed if the Garou are to win or simply survive. There is very much an intergenerational struggle going on. And of course, there were Ronin Garou who were the Caitiff of the setting. So there is totally supposed to be an equivalent of the Anarchs in the sense of discontented youth wanting to make change.<br /> <br /> I think that doesn't get traction for several reasons. The first is that fairly quickly the fans decide the Garou were good guy superheroes and effectively jettisoned the complications of Garou society. If you portray the Garou as good guys, then you undercut the need for &quot;Anarchs&quot; to change the system.<br /> <br /> The second is that the renown system really affected how players portrayed their characters. In order to get the higher level Gifts, you need the higher level ranks. And to get the ranks, you need the Renown. And by following the Renown, you end up being good Garou. Now it is totally possible to figure out a way for corrupt Garou to game the system, or for discontented &quot;Anarch&quot; type characters to still gain Renown. But we're never told within the game itself how that happens so the players don't have models on how to run it in their games. So they default to being sincere.<br /> <br /> A third is that in concentrating on the tribes and the difference between the tribes, we don't get any sense of how these young, discontented Garou organize or protest or just complain. There isn't an &quot;anarch&quot; camp in any of the tribes, nor a multi-tribal camp. So the game actually doesn't have any examples for PCs to model themselves on. So many players don't. They gravitate to the models that are provided which mostly support the system.<br /> <br /> For example, in none of the online or LARP games I've played, I never see examples of bad leadership at the sept. I don't see bad elders obviously failing, yet clinging onto power. I don't see the Bone Gnawer PCs acting up and complaining about the Garou leadership or Pure Breed that I always see with Brujah or Anarch PCs in online or LARP vampire games.<br /> <br /> While I do see PCs criticizing certain aspects of the setting, it's more theoretical because those things being criticized aren't actually portrayed by any of the NPCs or PCs of that chronicle. Silver Fang PCs aren't entitled assholes. Shadow Lord PCs aren't treacherous, ambitious pieces of shit. Bone Gnawers aren't self-serving jaded jerks that don't give a fuck. Glass Walkers aren't heretical Garou with very different ideas on what it means to be Gaian. Instead, there's a very strong conformity of everyone honestly trying to serve the sept. And I think it's mainly Renown that is causing it. The desire to &quot;level up&quot; means everyone behaves. To the point that even STs don't have NPCs act in ways the setting implies many NPCs act.<br /> <br /> So there's a disconnect between the setting as original portrayed and the mechanics in the game of how one increases in power. That's why Ronin never get played. In contrast, Vampire divorces status from the ability to increase in power, so I see a much wider variety of play styles and character concepts.<br /> <br /> I don't think that means that Renown has to change. We just need concrete examples of viable character concepts and how they were still able to rise in Renown and gain Rank so they can get the better Gifts. How can certain Garou rig the system to advance faster than they should? How can characters wanting to defy their elders and drive change in society still able to rise in Rank? Once players have other models, they'll start roleplaying in a more variety of ways.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T23:48:39-07:00","id":1465482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465469#post1465469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when I read some of the creator's ideas and your interpretation of it it gives me a bitter taste in my mouth. I feel that someone thinks that me and my players are too dumb to play with some toys so they will take them away from us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the issue: there's been generations of people that talk about their approach like you do, but then use it to abuse their fellow players. There's far too many gamers out there that read what you wrote and no matter how much you and your gaming circle are awesome people, would avoid you like the plague because you talk just like complete toxic asshats.<br /> <br /> It's not about how dumb anyone is. At worst it's that you have the benefit of not experience this for yourselves.<br /> <br /> It's about how insidious toxic elements of our communities can be. Lines like &quot;it's their problem if they can't handle it,&quot; is classic abusive language; there's a reason why victim blaming is a common tactic, and that's because it unfortunately works. I know dozens of gamers that have the bad kind of horror stories around STs that &quot;bend&quot; the line by splitting semantic hairs instead of respecting the spirit of a line a player draws (I know a ST that I've cut ties with for not recognizing that a player asking for no rape clearly meant no coerced consent, and that getting the player character to say &quot;yes&quot; without wanting to is still rape). If people can't tell the honest from the bad faith, they're just going to avoid both.<br /> <br /> As I've said, and others have said: it's easier to add than subtract. It's easier to make a game that's not aimed at people like you, but at people that want some more guard rails built into the game, and ask you to ignore those limitations, than it is to rely on our community to put those protections in after the fact. That's just the way it is.<br /> <br /> This is not about you, this is about all the shits out there that use people like you to hide their bad actions behind the respect you've earned by being able to maturely handle your style of play. You bitter taste at being stuck in the middle should be pointed at the people making things a problem instead of the people trying to address it as well as can be within their power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465479#post1465479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't an &quot;anarch&quot; camp in any of the tribes, nor a multi-tribal camp. So the game actually doesn't have any examples for PCs to model themselves on. So many players don't. They gravitate to the models that are provided which mostly support the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's... quite a number of Camps that might not be full on Anarchs, but certainly act as models for the conflict in question. The Silver Fangs have the most obvious examples of all Tribes: The Renewalist vs. Traditionalist factions.<br /> <br /> I think the bigger problem is that the Garou have such a more diverse political landscape than how VtM was set up. There aren't (rather unrealistic) lines where major factions break down so easily into political movements.<br /> <br /> The Bone Gnawers range heavily from barely members of the Garou Nation but don't want to be Ronin, to members trying to work with the Children of Gaia and Glass Walkers to get more respect for the &quot;lower&quot; Tribes. The Rat's Teeth are kinda the default Gnawer PCs because they actually see the value in working with the other Tribes directly; giving them reputations as both important to the Tribe not all getting cast out as Ronin, and sell outs to the rest of the Garou that see them all as scum.<br /> <br /> That sort of nuance can't be done in the simple Anarch vs. Cam conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, in none of the online or LARP games I've played, I never see examples of bad leadership at the sept. I don't see bad elders obviously failing, yet clinging onto power. I don't see the Bone Gnawer PCs acting up and complaining about the Garou leadership or Pure Breed that I always see with Brujah or Anarch PCs in online or LARP vampire games. </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of reasons here.<br /> <br /> I've been part of games where we've trying to facilitate this sort of dynamic:<br /> <br /> 1) Garou society, being more militaristic, is more regimented. Cliaths can't challenge Adren (or higher) no matter how much of a screw up the Adren really is. Which means you need to go above the Adren in the chain of command and find someone higher Rank to do something about it. This leads to massive strain on how the Sept leadership is even functional. Sure the players can get rid of one broken stair or something, but if you want this conflict to continue past one plot arc, other higher ranks and Sept officers have to have been in on it (at least to the point of actively turning a blind eye to it) until either the PCs have no chance against an ingrained Sept that is unified against them even if they're right, or by the time you've cleaned up all the corruption and nepotism and so on, there's so little Sept left that it can't operate effectively any more.<br /> <br /> 2) Players don't like to keep going on IC about stuff that they can't change. Well bred Garou can't be made to be less well bred. There's no way to turn off their bonuses. A Gnawer with PB 0 vs. a Silver Fang with PB 5 sitting around grumbling all the time isn't something players want to engage with because that's the rules, so the Gnawer (and Walker, and etc.) players just move on because they'd rather be proactive and thus more fun to play with.<br /> <br /> 3) As you went into with Renown, the game has a lot of places where rocking the boat just isn't a good idea. An Elder can still face consequences if they travel to a level 5 Caern to learn a new Rank 5 Gift, but don't pay their proper respect to the local Sept and its customs. This leads to a lot more, &quot;work within to push for change,&quot; than full on Anarch style counter-movements.<br /> <br /> 4) Between 13 Tribes, 5 Auspices, and 3 Breeds, the Garou just don't need political faction to be an essential part of character variety. There's a lot of dynamics already in play that are, to many players, interesting enough without trying to copy early WtA's stronger affinity for retreading VtM's political conflicts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T15:08:47-07:00","id":1465570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465478#post1465478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The killing of disabled people isn't exclusive to specific populations with poor education and specific superstitions. It happens in every nation at alarming rates, along with many other forms of mistreatment.<br /> <br /> Comparing the mistreatment of disabled people specifically with such a specific stance gives a wrong idea of the subject and is, in itself, offensive to the many victims that remain invisible in &amp;quot;educated&amp;quot; societies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Albino hunts is just one example. I mentioned it because one of my favourite polish journalists wrote an article about it. I am fully aware that Nazis or Spartans did the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-27T16:11:14-07:00","id":1465573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465482#post1465482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's the issue: there's been generations of people that talk about their approach like you do, but then use it to abuse their fellow players. There's far too many gamers out there that read what you wrote and no matter how much you and your gaming circle are awesome people, would avoid you like the plague because you talk just like complete toxic asshats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touche. I personally know a few. But still I think that there are better ways to handle that than using the hatchet. As for avoiding me like a plague still it's not my problem. I really don't need people who escape from confronting with other's people values. The thing is that there as many opinions as there are people. I may not agree with many of them but I will defend their right to have them as long as it isn't a threat. Fun fact: if you close your eyes or run away from problems they won't disappear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465482#post1465482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about how dumb anyone is. At worst it's that you have the benefit of not experience this for yourselves.<br /> <br /> It's about how insidious toxic elements of our communities can be. Lines like &quot;it's their problem if they can't handle it,&quot; is classic abusive language; there's a reason why victim blaming is a common tactic, and that's because it unfortunately works. I know dozens of gamers that have the bad kind of horror stories around STs that &quot;bend&quot; the line by splitting semantic hairs instead of respecting the spirit of a line a player draws (I know a ST that I've cut ties with for not recognizing that a player asking for no rape clearly meant no coerced consent, and that getting the player character to say &quot;yes&quot; without wanting to is still rape). If people can't tell the honest from the bad faith, they're just going to avoid both.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with you about blaming the victims. I was bullied at school and still I think that this was partially my and my parent's fault. My parents made me (genetically) the youngest, smallest and quite smart kid. Perfect target, right? I also could hide my intellect but what's the point. Instead I started to train. Ok, I was still the smallest one but with a few years of boxing under my belt I stood my ground. Not always (and most of the times not) victorious but I could look in the mirror without disgust. And I waited. Karma did the rest: one of my abusers ended in a loveless marriage (and his parents, quite rich, told him that they will disown him if he will ever divorce), the other one (from another affluent family) is a homeless alcoholic. I got a good job I like (but on the other hand I used to do more fascinating jobs), I'm in a quite happy relationship, I am healthy and got a family who supports me. So I feel sorry for all those who let somebody cloud their opinion about themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465482#post1465482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I've said, and others have said: it's easier to add than subtract. It's easier to make a game that's not aimed at people like you, but at people that want some more guard rails built into the game, and ask you to ignore those limitations, than it is to rely on our community to put those protections in after the fact. That's just the way it is.<br /> <br /> This is not about you, this is about all the shits out there that use people like you to hide their bad actions behind the respect you've earned by being able to maturely handle your style of play. You bitter taste at being stuck in the middle should be pointed at the people making things a problem instead of the people trying to address it as well as can be within their power.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we are talking about substracting. The others have said: if we allow Garou mate with other Garou without consequences then the kinfolks will be mostly useless. I say that if we eliminate metis breed the Garou society will be poorer. Imagine Sept of the Green without Fengy, in my opinion one of the most interesting SPCs. Imagine my former PCs hopelesly trying to save a member of their pack from himself; he was an abused metis who, with each day, was closer to the mouth of Wyrm. Imagine my game without a banished maneater metis, who was thrown out from his sept because of that. It was not his fault, spirits made him a cannibal. And what about my favourite SPC, a Ragabash who claimed that in the Last Days every Garou should sire a metis (to produce Gaia's warriors), then at least one litter of lupus (to increase the possibility of creating another Garou) and then move to homid kinfolk (he adressed the homids most of the time). But I will wait (as usual). Maybe the creators can defend that idea. But for Gaia's sake not because some players can find metis treatment offensive but because of some kind of divine intervention. Because Gaia wills it, not because they will it. And still we should remember that most tribes grudgingly accept metis. Children of Gaia and Bone Gnawers allow to join almost any of them, most of the others at least give them a chance (with more or less difficulties). I think that only Wendigo and Get of Fenris (and of course Red Talons, but from different reasons) would not accept them.<br /> <br /> Imho the best way to handle it would be creating a branch that will handle the most controversive topic. Just like Black Dog used to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 10-28-2021, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T05:08:53-07:00","id":1465621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465573#post1465573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact: if you close your eyes or run away from problems they won't disappear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends what your problems are.<br /> <br /> As I've said, we're talking about a game. A game meant for people to sit around (in some fashion or another) an have a good time pretending to be characters in a fictional universe. If we want to close our eyes and pretend something we agree is offensive isn't there, it isn't, because we're playing a game of cooperative imagination and if we all imagine it away, it isn't part of our game any more.<br /> <br /> Of course, that doesn't mean it isn't part of our lives in general, put sometimes a few hours without things we have to deal with outside of leisure time is a good thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was bullied at school and still I think that this was partially my and my parent's fault. </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. Bullying is a fairly complicate social behavior to address, but in the end it's a societal problem. The western model of schools and other common adolescent social environments is practically tailor made to encourage bullying. Generations of normalization to this approach is far beyond any individual lay blame on; esp. the targets of bullying. If we wanted a society where bullying is practically non-existent, it's not hard to construct. The problems are a combination of convincing people to change, and convincing people that the costs are worth it (which is often a large stumbling block when it comes to kids).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Karma did the rest: </div> </div> </div>A pleasing narrative, but how many of them would have had different lives if they hadn't bullied you? Do you think a single one of them, in some moment of self-reflection, would ever think, &quot;if only I'd been a nicer kid in school, my life would be great?&quot; Seems far fetched to me.<br /> <br /> There's also plenty of kids the get bullied and don't get to have a nice story about how reality vindicated them. Our stories aren't that different, but most of the kids that bullied me in school are living way nicer lives than I am. Karma isn't a great explanation if it's not even in its justice (and of course the full spiritual concept of karma is a lot more complicated than pithy Internet posts generally abide).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But we are talking about substracting. </div> </div> </div>Well, for the most part, we're talking about multiple orders of speculation based on a very limited amount of actual information.<br /> <br /> As well, whether subtracting is worth the effort over addition in the design phase of games is a very different calculus than what sort of subtracting/adding the game presents to players as options once the game is released.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The others have said: if we allow Garou mate with other Garou without consequences then the kinfolks will be mostly useless. </div> </div> </div>That's solely a matter of execution. If Garou can have as much sex as they want with other Garou, but they'll never get pregnant from it... well Kinfolk are still just as important before and after that change; but it makes that part of the Litany unimportant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I say that if we eliminate metis breed the Garou society will be poorer. </div> </div> </div>As I've gone into more detail elsewhere. My position is that fixing the Garou-born should be done before cutting them, but I don't see a strong argument that cutting them is worse than leaving them in as they are.<br /> <br /> Outside of tautological examples, there's no concepts that just have to be Garou-born to make them work. Homids can be the products of illicit affairs. They can be extremely short. They can have attachment issues that give them trouble finding a place in Garou society after growing up outside of it. Etc You can make a Fengy that does the important narrative role Fengy inhabits with a different Breed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because Gaia wills it, not because they will it </div> </div> </div>Gaia, in this context, isn't real. Gaia's will is the developer's will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that only Wendigo and Get of Fenris (and of course Red Talons, but from different reasons) would not accept them. </div> </div> </div>The Fianna and Silver Fangs are traditionally the most anti-tolerance Tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imho the best way to handle it would be creating a branch that will handle the most controversive topic. Just like Black Dog used to do. </div> </div> </div>Black Dog really wasn't that effective. The good Black Dog books felt diminished by being shunted off to a &quot;lesser&quot; label, while the bad ones felt sensationalized by the notoriety of the same label (like slapping a Parental Advisory Warning sticker on something was a great way to get kids to buy it for being transgressive instead of for quality content).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":".  silly typo even if I think most people realized it. 10-28-2021, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T06:54:44-07:00","id":1465643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465573#post1465573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for avoiding me like a plague still it's not my problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the writers'.<br /> <br /> As much as I agree that ditching the Metis is a bad decision, I do so out of very different reasons. You didn't get what I meant about disabled people being killed, either.<br /> <br /> Your life went great, resorting to violence worked for you and you got vindicated by God. Good for you. Is not everyone's experience, though, and you can't put your enjoyment over testing social limits above other people's suffering, much less blaming them for being &quot;incapable of handling it&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy gripe with handling the Metis this way is that the idea of elimination is the worst of two evils to me. What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> is talking about is deadly serious, but is also kind of a shitty situation with no easy way out. For some people this is a PTSD trigger. It causes very real pain and suffering, when a game should be an enjoyable moment. For others it may be uncomfortable in many other ways.<br /> <br /> But the Metis also makes the theme easier to approach when a player wants to, and this is a valuable valve. It formalizes disabilities as a thing in the setting even if you don't have one at your table. This gave us visibility and participation, protagonism. It also works both ways, people that want to bring the theme to the table have an easier time, people that tend to forget it are reminded of it, but people that want to act like jerks because of their ableism feel entitled to do so. It is good and it sucks.<br /> <br /> How's the best way to handle it? Hard to tell, we have disabled posters here on both sides of the debate. In my opinion, it is like Forsaken did: do not do it like that in the first place. It didn't worked as intended and we have to find another way. But now this is not an option, the Metis are in Apocalypse's history one way or another, and in my opinion just getting them out leaves a very, very bitter taste in the mouth.<br /> <br /> Whatever the future holds, we have to face this problem as actual adults that can try to weigh in the different problems and find a good compromise, even if it means a different game to play, not as wannabe adults that hide behind victim-blaming to not change anything that isn't affecting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T10:39:47-07:00","id":1466148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465621#post1465621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends what your problems are.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of them will, imaginary or not<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465621#post1465621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it isn't. Bullying is a fairly complicate social behavior to address, but in the end it's a societal problem. The western model of schools and other common adolescent social environments is practically tailor made to encourage bullying. Generations of normalization to this approach is far beyond any individual lay blame on; esp. the targets of bullying. If we wanted a society where bullying is practically non-existent, it's not hard to construct. The problems are a combination of convincing people to change, and convincing people that the costs are worth it (which is often a large stumbling block when it comes to kids).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you didn't get it. I said this ironically. But I can assure you that blaming my parents is partially accurate. If I was born bigger and stronger bullies wouldn't touch me. They would be scared.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465621#post1465621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A pleasing narrative, but how many of them would have had different lives if they hadn't bullied you? Do you think a single one of them, in some moment of self-reflection, would ever think, &amp;quot;if only I'd been a nicer kid in school, my life would be great?&amp;quot; Seems far fetched to me.<br /> <br /> There's also plenty of kids the get bullied and don't get to have a nice story about how reality vindicated them. Our stories aren't that different, but most of the kids that bullied me in school are living way nicer lives than I am. Karma isn't a great explanation if it's not even in its justice (and of course the full spiritual concept of karma is a lot more complicated than pithy Internet posts generally abide).</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they wouldn't. They were strong (especially working as a team), but none of them was too bright. As for other kids I just don't get it. Everybody says &quot;it's you who are important, believe in yourself&quot; and they still allow bullies mess with their self respect. &quot;God helps those who help themselves&quot;. That's why I started boxing. If someone want to let others harass them so be it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465621#post1465621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for the most part, we're talking about multiple orders of speculation based on a very limited amount of actual information.<br /> <br /> As well, whether subtracting is worth the effort over addition in the design phase of games is a very different calculus than what sort of subtracting/adding the game presents to players as options once the game is released.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I will wait<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465621#post1465621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's solely a matter of execution. If Garou can have as much sex as they want with other Garou, but they'll never get pregnant from it... well Kinfolk are still just as important before and after that change; but it makes that part of the Litany unimportant.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it was there always. There should be an explanation, better than &quot;just because&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465621#post1465621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I've gone into more detail elsewhere. My position is that fixing the Garou-born should be done before cutting them, but I don't see a strong argument that cutting them is worse than leaving them in as they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you shouldn't everybody mess with your work. I think it's a matter of political corectness. Rockstar Games don't give a f\u20ac&quot;k about it and their games still are bestsellers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465621#post1465621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Outside of tautological examples, there's no concepts that just have to be Garou-born to make them work. Homids can be the products of illicit affairs. They can be extremely short. They can have attachment issues that give them trouble finding a place in Garou society after growing up outside of it. Etc You can make a Fengy that does the important narrative role Fengy inhabits with a different Breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be hard. He was born short and was left in the severs. He was hiding for many years (that's why his knowledge of NY is legendary) before being found. If it wasn't the shame his parents felt (ex. if he was born Homid) it wouldn't be so. Also as much as he wants to be helpful he is a big coward so this also give him some depth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465621#post1465621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gaia, in this context, isn't real. Gaia's will is the developer's will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again you didn't get it. I mean they should explain that, and not do something like &quot;I want that because it's politically correct&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465621#post1465621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fianna and Silver Fangs are traditionally the most anti-tolerance Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can agree with SF, Fianna are intolerant but for parents, not the child.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1465621#post1465621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Dog really wasn't that effective. The good Black Dog books felt diminished by being shunted off to a &amp;quot;lesser&amp;quot; label, while the bad ones felt sensationalized by the notoriety of the same label (like slapping a Parental Advisory Warning sticker on something was a great way to get kids to buy it for being transgressive instead of for quality content).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but still I think it's worth a try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T11:56:31-07:00","id":1466150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466148#post1466148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of them will, imaginary or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the assertion the imaginary problems don't go away if you stop imagining them very odd. It can certainly be easier said than done regarding all sorts of problems that only exist in our heads, but cooperative fiction gaming is a construct we consciously control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you didn't get it. </div> </div> </div>It's always possible I'm not fully understanding your intended meaning, but I feel like I have a fairly solid grasp on bullying from a variety of perspectives having dealt with it as a victim and as an adult responsible for reducing it within my little corner of the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I can assure you that blaming my parents is partially accurate. If I was born bigger and stronger bullies wouldn't touch me. They would be scared. </div> </div> </div>Your parents have no reasonable control over such things. Height and muscle mass in humans is not some simple single gene Mendelian cross. We're talking about the interaction of dozens of genes and epigenetic factors. There's literally hundreds (many of which are fairly rare) of ways a tiny random mutation can cause a radical difference in expected height or muscle mass from looking at parental phenotypes.<br /> <br /> My mother actually specifically dated taller men hoping to have taller children as someone that's rather short (even if within average range). It &quot;worked&quot; in that I'm the same height as my father, but I also grew 1.5 feet between 16 and 18 (and most of that towards the later half). I spent all of middle school and most of high-school tiny. My genetics of &quot;average&quot; finally kicked in far too late to avoid bullying based on my size.<br /> <br /> And even then? If we ever get past both the practical/technological and ethical issues with genetically engineering children? We're still going to have bullying if nothing else changes, because access and quality of technological interventions are not evenly divided. Kids from rich and connected families will get better gene editing, and then use that to pick on the poorer kids that had access to worse gene editing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, they wouldn't. </div> </div> </div>Then it's not much Karma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for other kids I just don't get it. Everybody says &quot;it's you who are important, believe in yourself&quot; and they still allow bullies mess with their self respect. &quot;God helps those who help themselves&quot;. </div> </div> </div>You don't seem to get the massive spectrum of responses to bullying, and what the practical range of responses are for any given child. You are you. What worked for you isn't inherently going to work for everyone else. I don't see why this is a difficult concept.<br /> <br /> Lets take a simple example: Footwork is essential for boxing (or any other combat sport/self defense training a kid is likely to have access to). Without solid foot work, your punches are going to be slow and weak, your defense is going to be paper thin, and you're going to get knocked on your ass with ease. Boxing isn't going to help the self-esteem of kids that have impairments that mean they're physically incapable of keeping up with even the most basic footwork training.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There should be an explanation, better than &quot;just because&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Because Gaia wants the Garou to be tied to humans and wolves, not just each other. That's already in the game. It's just changing how it's enforced for the Garou. The Gurhal, for instance, are basically already this solution. Werebear on werewbear sex is largely pointless from a reproductive standpoint, so they mate with humans and bears.<br /> <br /> Doubting there's going to be a metaplot level explanation is rather unfounded. Distrusting the quality of it in our expectations is a different matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because you shouldn't everybody mess with your work. </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between &quot;letting everybody mess with your work,&quot; and listening to audience feedback with consideration. If a company feels that there's far more fan support for a change than against is, and even has solid indications that the change is necessary to appeal to a wider audience, making the change isn't &quot;politically correct&quot; it's business correct. Though you have to do it well.<br /> <br /> There are lots of elements of the WoD that range for, &quot;this aged very poorly,&quot; to, &quot;fans have been vocally complaining about this for almost 30 years,&quot; it would be malpractice to not even examine such topics at a design level when starting a new edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's a matter of political corectness. </div> </div> </div>Define political correctness in a fashion that doesn't amount to, &quot;the speaker doesn't like it, but recognizes there's a significant number of people pushing for it, and needs a label to avoid engaging with any points made in disagreement.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rockstar Games don't give a f\u20ac&quot;k about it and their games still are bestsellers. </div> </div> </div>Video games are an entirely different market. RPGs are a tiny niche market with a very small audience. Even with the cultural popularity of D&amp;D, it's still not something you can really compare. Your average Rockstar Games production has a budget that's bigger than the production budgets of every RPG book made in a year outside of D&amp;D combined. That's the orders of magnitudes apart we're talking about. Rockstar can carve out a niche for itself as a maker of politically incorrect and shocking/edgy games, because the video game industry is so big that niche is still massive sales.<br /> <br /> Of course, Rockstar does actually &quot;give a fuck,&quot; as even they know they have lines they can't cross. There's stuff that they cut from games because they knew it was going too far even for GTA. They also know that their main audience has lead to them getting a bit pigeonholed as Bully suffered significantly - not because of the expected backlash over calling a video game about kids &quot;Bully which they were ready for - from their existing fans that got pissed of that the main character of Bully could experiment with another guy.<br /> <br /> And, of course, there's just the apples and oranges comparison here.<br /> <br /> GTA is farce. It's meant to be an over the top crazy escapist violent power fantasy. The Red Dead series is not. There's a reason there's a lot of stuff you can do in GTA that will never show up in a Red Dead game. They're different games with different designs and different lines on what will and will not get made for them.<br /> <br /> The WoD is it's own game, with its own considerations. The WoD has always been a highly political set of games, and that means getting the politics right; or correct if you will. If you want to have a strong political message in your RPG, you're going to get judged in how you execute it. If you want a more GTA-like RPG? Those exist, but they're not the WoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would be hard. </div> </div> </div>The hardest part of all of Fengy's background is how utterly ridiculous some of it is if you actually think about what getting tossed in a NYC sewer as a baby would mean, even in Crinos, and the idea that it would give you legendary knowledge of anything other than the smells of garbage, feces, and urine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...Fianna are intolerant but for parents, not the child. </div> </div> </div>Not according to the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, but still I think it's worth a try. </div> </div> </div>Based on what? Where has this worked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T13:12:44-07:00","id":1466158,"title":"","content":"I totally get it that I should just grow over my Autism and become a worse threat than the bullies instead of expecting sensible adults to work at making a better environment for kids. It was my fault, and my parents for making me Autistic.<br /> <br /> What I should do by now is play a game where everything bad that already happens to me or other Autistics and Disabled people stays happening again and again without ever becoming better, so I can steel myself and get the will to learn a martial art, then punch assholes in the streets and at the workplace.<br /> <br /> My problems won't go away during a game, the only correct way to play is to keep living them. After all it isn't about healthy fun, it is about treating my players like trash as life does, so they can overcome it all with violence.<br /> <br /> Although I do enjoy roleplaying all those ugly sides of life, even of my actual life, I never enjoy playing in the same group as a jerks that use wordplay and victim-blaming to make the other players uncomfortable instead of the characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T14:06:38-07:00","id":1466166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466150#post1466150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your parents have no reasonable control over such things. Height and muscle mass in humans is not some simple single gene Mendelian cross. We're talking about the interaction of dozens of genes and epigenetic factors. There's literally hundreds (many of which are fairly rare) of ways a tiny random mutation can cause a radical difference in expected height or muscle mass from looking at parental phenotypes.<br /> <br /> My mother actually specifically dated taller men hoping to have taller children as someone that's rather short (even if within average range). It &amp;quot;worked&amp;quot; in that I'm the same height as my father, but I also grew 1.5 feet between 16 and 18 (and most of that towards the later half). I spent all of middle school and most of high-school tiny. My genetics of &amp;quot;average&amp;quot; finally kicked in far too late to avoid bullying based on my size.<br /> <br /> And even then? If we ever get past both the practical/technological and ethical issues with genetically engineering children? We're still going to have bullying if nothing else changes, because access and quality of technological interventions are not evenly divided. Kids from rich and connected families will get better gene editing, and then use that to pick on the poorer kids that had access to worse gene editing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaand you still don't understand. Or misread my post on purpose. So I try other way:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irony\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b5/Situational_irony_-_Baker_Street_tube_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irony\" target=\"_blank\"> Irony - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irony\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irony </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarcasm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Advertisement_for_fitness_studio_in_Germany.jpeg/960px-Advertisement_for_fitness_studio_in_Germany.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarcasm\" target=\"_blank\"> Sarcasm - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarcasm\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarcasm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466150#post1466150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't seem to get the massive spectrum of responses to bullying, and what the practical range of responses are for any given child. You are you. What worked for you isn't inherently going to work for everyone else. I don't see why this is a difficult concept.<br /> <br /> Lets take a simple example: Footwork is essential for boxing (or any other combat sport/self defense training a kid is likely to have access to). Without solid foot work, your punches are going to be slow and weak, your defense is going to be paper thin, and you're going to get knocked on your ass with ease. Boxing isn't going to help the self-esteem of kids that have impairments that mean they're physically incapable of keeping up with even the most basic footwork training.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you look yourself in a mirror if you didn't even try? I couldn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466150#post1466150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Gaia wants the Garou to be tied to humans and wolves, not just each other. That's already in the game. It's just changing how it's enforced for the Garou. The Gurhal, for instance, are basically already this solution. Werebear on werewbear sex is largely pointless from a reproductive standpoint, so they mate with humans and bears.<br /> <br /> Doubting there's going to be a metaplot level explanation is rather unfounded. Distrusting the quality of it in our expectations is a different matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I saw what Disney did to Star Wars, throwing all books away. I believe this is a good reason not to trust new WoD publisher<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466150#post1466150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a difference between &amp;quot;letting everybody mess with your work,&amp;quot; and listening to audience feedback with consideration. If a company feels that there's far more fan support for a change than against is, and even has solid indications that the change is necessary to appeal to a wider audience, making the change isn't &amp;quot;politically correct&amp;quot; it's business correct. Though you have to do it well.<br /> <br /> There are lots of elements of the WoD that range for, &amp;quot;this aged very poorly,&amp;quot; to, &amp;quot;fans have been vocally complaining about this for almost 30 years,&amp;quot; it would be malpractice to not even examine such topics at a design level when starting a new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all I meant anybody. And about complaints being the majority doesn't mean that you are right. If majority votes for mass suicide would you still think we should follow them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466150#post1466150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Define political correctness in a fashion that doesn't amount to, &amp;quot;the speaker doesn't like it, but recognizes there's a significant number of people pushing for it, and needs a label to avoid engaging with any points made in disagreement.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I got nothing against political corectness. It's about going too far in that. What is offensive in calling people by colour of their skin? I'm caucasian so this means white. Afroamericans have darker skin tone. And I heard voices that I'm racist because I noticed that. I can understand that calling someone fatty could be offensive, but I don't understand why calling the same person overweight is offensive too. No, now it's plus size (of course the size is 50). But being (politically correct) plus size don't eliminate your problems with heart, joints etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466150#post1466150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Video games are an entirely different market. RPGs are a tiny niche market with a very small audience. Even with the cultural popularity of D&amp;D, it's still not something you can really compare. Your average Rockstar Games production has a budget that's bigger than the production budgets of every RPG book made in a year outside of D&amp;D combined. That's the orders of magnitudes apart we're talking about. Rockstar can carve out a niche for itself as a maker of politically incorrect and shocking/edgy games, because the video game industry is so big that niche is still massive sales.<br /> <br /> Of course, Rockstar does actually &amp;quot;give a fuck,&amp;quot; as even they know they have lines they can't cross. There's stuff that they cut from games because they knew it was going too far even for GTA. They also know that their main audience has lead to them getting a bit pigeonholed as Bully suffered significantly - not because of the expected backlash over calling a video game about kids &amp;quot;Bully which they were ready for - from their existing fans that got pissed of that the main character of Bully could experiment with another guy.<br /> <br /> And, of course, there's just the apples and oranges comparison here.<br /> <br /> GTA is farce. It's meant to be an over the top crazy escapist violent power fantasy. The Red Dead series is not. There's a reason there's a lot of stuff you can do in GTA that will never show up in a Red Dead game. They're different games with different designs and different lines on what will and will not get made for them.<br /> <br /> The WoD is it's own game, with its own considerations. The WoD has always been a highly political set of games, and that means getting the politics right; or correct if you will. If you want to have a strong political message in your RPG, you're going to get judged in how you execute it. If you want a more GTA-like RPG? Those exist, but they're not the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but why not make a few options and let the players and storytellers decide?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466150#post1466150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The hardest part of all of Fengy's background is how utterly ridiculous some of it is if you actually think about what getting tossed in a NYC sewer as a baby would mean, even in Crinos, and the idea that it would give you legendary knowledge of anything other than the smells of garbage, feces, and urine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fengy instinctively changed his form into lupus, join the pack of stray dogs and that's how he got this knowledge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466150#post1466150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not according to the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, this I remembered incorectly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466150#post1466150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Based on what? Where has this worked?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it worked. I said it's worth a try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T14:18:00-07:00","id":1466168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466158#post1466158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally get it that I should just grow over my Autism and become a worse threat than the bullies instead of expecting sensible adults to work at making a better environment for kids. It was my fault, and my parents for making me Autistic.<br /> <br /> What I should do by now is play a game where everything bad that already happens to me or other Autistics and Disabled people stays happening again and again without ever becoming better, so I can steel myself and get the will to learn a martial art, then punch assholes in the streets and at the workplace.<br /> <br /> My problems won't go away during a game, the only correct way to play is to keep living them. After all it isn't about healthy fun, it is about treating my players like trash as life does, so they can overcome it all with violence.<br /> <br /> Although I do enjoy roleplaying all those ugly sides of life, even of my actual life, I never enjoy playing in the same group as a jerks that use wordplay and victim-blaming to make the other players uncomfortable instead of the characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you also didn't understand what I was trying to say. My parents made me a comfortable environement. It was my father who bought me my first boxing gloves and show me the basic moves. It wasn't about violence, it was self defence and, I have to admit, giving them a bit of things they served me. I just don't get how anybody can allow others instill they point of view about themselves. It's how you see yourself, not how others see you. If you challenge yourself and win, overcoming all obstacles, there's no force in the universe that can make you feel like a failure. If you see yourself as a champion then you are a champion. And I know many people who should be proud of themselves and still has low self esteem. I just don't get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T15:13:29-07:00","id":1466179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466168#post1466168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point. That's the whole point.<br /> <br /> People have different mindsets, different reactions, different ways to digest what happen to them, and sometimes different biochemistry entirely. They don't process feelings and thoughts in the same way.<br /> <br /> Your problem here is that you get from <i>your</i>experience without realizing that the world is full of people that don't work the same way, yet we must make it work for everyone, or weigh down were the least harm will be done.<br /> <br /> I can't understand you more than you can understand me. And that while, as I said, I'm not personally the kind of person that would mind your way of running the game, except for the OoC aspect. But we don't understand how it is to have PTSD or other intense Anxiety Disorders, either.<br /> <br /> A lot of people simply won't deal with the same problems the same way. A lot of problems aren't the same even if they seem so in the surface. I don't have to understand all of them, I have to know and accept this reality and move on to actual solutions to problems.<br /> <br /> What do we solve putting the onus on the victim, except nothing? People who can't just &quot;try&quot; won't change because you said they should. They'll feel an even greater failure, maybe, at most. How possible it was for you won't change that they can't. Saying that children facing bullying should defend themselves will change what if most of them just don't have the means, either external or internal, to try?<br /> <br /> Not to say that we are <b>not</b> talking about bullying, and your focus on this just shows how off the target you are on the matter. Ableism is something that affects a person's entire life. It is not about self-esteem.<br /> <br /> My self-esteem is fine, yet I'm stuck at the bottom of my career with little prospect of growth because a promotion depends entirely on other people's perception about me. This is the situation of many disabled workers. Some at my company hide their conditions, exposing themselves to their unique health hazards, so they don't get the same treatment and can be actually promoted. But the reality is that disabled people, even after accounting for their actual limitations, have a hugely harder time getting work, so I'm actually extremely well positioned because I have a stable job to begin with.<br /> <br /> Before I talked about deaths. Disabled people are targeted in several ways and this is <b>not</b> limited to any particular country or social strata. It isn't just something that happens at East Africa or something. This happens right now, everywhere, even at Poland. Outside deaths there are several other health and life threatening situations a disabled person must face frequently because of ableism, as people completely disregard their different necessities.<br /> <br /> Finally, even if it <b>was </b>just self-esteem, you're completely oblivious to how it can play at others' lives. You have no idea how it is to suffer gaslighting almost all the time, everywhere. And guess what: hearing a person's limits and them using wordplay to &quot;bend&quot; those limits <b><u>is</u></b> gaslighting. A problem so serious that can lead to suicide.<br /> <br /> Don't try to understand people that can't &quot;try&quot;. Even because you don't even know if they really didn't, just because they're not in the same mental place as you. Just accept them and do your part in making the gaming environment better for people that needs it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T15:47:18-07:00","id":1466186,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Nail Eater, you're touching on a lot of real life mental issues and this has nothing to do with the subject. Please drop it.<br /> <br /> In fact, please move on from this topic as a whole, everyone.</span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https