d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T04:43:34-07:00","id":1466441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466431#post1466431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean we don't even know why they're getting rid of metis as brutally shown here representation issues are a minefield so that might not be it.<br /> It could be that they want more romantic options for players or even an eye to the furry fandoms fondness for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have to wait for their word on the matter, even if just to try and read in the subtext.<br /> <br /> \u200bOtherwise, one thing <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said extremely right: we don't know how they'll explain it in the setting, if they will. It is pointless to get angry at a lack of explanation that isn't actually a thing. We have every reason to keep a low expectation, but that isn't more than expectation yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T08:25:20-07:00","id":1466464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466441#post1466441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we don't know how they'll explain it in the setting, if they will. (...) We have every reason to keep a low expectation, but that isn't more than expectation yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that they should. Otherwise they will look like Disney, trashing all Star Wars expanded universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T11:19:39-07:00","id":1466498,"title":"","content":"Remembering how fraught comparing things to Disney's run with Star Wars has been:<br /> <br /> I don't see how the comparison works. Star Wars had, long before Disney, a hierarchy of canon. The movies were always at the top. When the prequels came out, they contradicted lots of EU stuff which was immediately rendered non-canon because that's how Lucas decided things would work. This is, generally speaking, a very strange set up in large media franchises (any that grow close to this sort of size opt for parallel canons like the Marvel comics vs. the MCU). Disney just opted to take advantage of the existing way Star Wars handled canon status to proactively put a bunch of the lower canon status EU works into the Legends category of non-canon.<br /> <br /> Whatever W5 does is going to be an apples-to-oranges situation to that because whatever happens with W5, it's not how Lucas setup canon to work in SW.<br /> <br /> This actually makes the situation worse; as we've seen with V5. In SW, there was a long standing public facing way to figure out what to do if setting material contradicts in different sources by labeling certain sources inherently more authoritative. In V5, there are some serious continuity issues because it is very fuzzy about how the past canon and the current canon interact. The editions are supposed to be in a single continuity, but there's a lot of unaddressed contradictions and no real guide in how to navigate them.<br /> <br /> SW fans might be pissed off that Disney decided that G-canon remains canon, T-canon is canon unless stated otherwise, and C-, S-, and D-canons are all rendered N-canon under the Legends header... but the very fact that sentence can be parsed to mean anything sensible undercuts a lot of outrage that isn't just a difference in preference over the direction of the franchise.<br /> <br /> WoD fans are already trying to navigate how to deal with all of the gray areas where V5 has changed things without explaining if these are retroactive changes, changes that have actually occurred due to metaplot events, or some other option.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T14:44:19-07:00","id":1466516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466498#post1466498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how the comparison works. Star Wars had, long before Disney, a hierarchy of canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>More importantly, Disney had actually a far more sensible approach to canon than George Lucas ever had, as he wasn't shy of retconing things and literally call off copies in the market to change for his &quot;improved&quot; versions.<br /> <br /> It's also a factor that Star Wars is a movie franchise, not an RPG franchise. The way the fan relate to the setting is completely different.<br /> <br /> So, Paradox should explain it in setting? Of fucking course. Will they? I don't know. But for now arguing that is pointless, and given that they went forward to publicly say that Metis aren't a thing anymore, it is likely that they will, and <b>when</b> they do we can discuss its quality.<br /> <br /> A very different approach from their take on the Kuei-Jin they apparently will just retcon out of existence. Apparently because since they're going to do this, their take on the matter is simply being as silent as possible, so even their few statements for people asking are just hearsay. Hearsay I do believe in, yet hearsay they can deny whenever they feel the need to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T21:23:36-07:00","id":1466607,"title":"","content":"Crimson Thaw 2 , tribe: Ghost Council. Wtf is that? Uktena??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T21:33:01-07:00","id":1466609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466607#post1466607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crimson Thaw 2 , tribe: Ghost Council. Wtf is that? Uktena??</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unsure. One of the characters has their tribe redacted but it seems to say Wendigo.<br /> <br /> At first blush I was thinking they were replacing both Older and Younger Brothers North American cohort with the Ghost Council.....but with that redacted element I'm unsure what they're doing.<br /> <br /> I have no issue replacing the names U and W, neither are appropriate as Tribal Names....but I'm not sure how I feel about both NA-origin Tribes being erased. If James Sambrano or a similar writer were still working on W5 I'd be intrigued and slightly optimistic....with the current W5 team I'm less so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T23:40:57-07:00","id":1466613,"title":"","content":"I can understand merging pure one tribes - Wendigo and Uktena in one, I could even swallow merging them with Silent Striders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T00:26:17-07:00","id":1466615,"title":"","content":"If Uktena and Wendigo are becoming one single tribe I suppose it has sense. I'm not sure about the Wendigos surviving the 90's with them going full-isolationists. At the same time, if they are merged with the Ukterna, I suppose now everyone can basically join them, as Achilli said, goodbye to ethnic-cultural boundaries. The character from Ghost Council is btw cearly indigenous american, at least, looks like it. Pretty multi-ethnic and multi tribal pack.<br /> <br /> But, why the hell a tribe name is not showed and it's marked in black in one of the garou profiles?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T00:59:28-07:00","id":1466617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463892-after-much-speculation-some-new-w5-official-information?p=1466615#post1466615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-ico